+  "body": "<p>Find ordinary equipment with the <a href=\"loot-finder.html\">Loot finder</a>, browse <a href=\"items.html\">Hunt rewards</a>, or compare an upgrade in the <a href=\"build-lab.html\">Build Lab</a>.</p><h2 id=\"free-trade\">Player trading and duplicate items</h2><p>Trade formerly NO DROP and NO TRANSFER items, already-attuned gear, bags, their contents and augments. <strong>LORE restrictions are disabled</strong>, so duplicate ownership is allowed. Inventory capacity, temporary-item expiration and Pet Armor restrictions remain. Equipment eligibility still depends on your held classes and the remaining item requirements.</p>\n<h2 id=\"item-tiers\">Polished, Exalted, and Ascended loot</h2><p>Eligible dropped equipment and bags can appear in three stronger custom tiers. Their health, mana, defenses, and offensive stats scale by item family.</p>\n<p>Ordinary eligible equipment and bags now roll <strong>20% Polished, 5% Exalted and 1% Ascended</strong>, leaving 74% Normal when all variants exist. These chances apply per eligible item drop, not per kill. Already generated loot is not rerolled. Zone-hunt and dungeon rewards keep their separate rates.</p><h2 id=\"zone-hunt\">Augments in50 Classic zones; gear in the original48</h2><p>Any unowned, killable NPC in an enabled augment zone can roll its augment, including guards, named and quest NPCs, killable merchants and scripted combat adds. Player-owned/charmed pets, mercenaries, swarm pets, protected noncombat actors and restored corpses do not reroll. Native corpse ownership and encounter access still apply. Augments roll at 1.5%; equipment sources keep their separate 0.5% chance and level/night restrictions. Qualities remain Base60%, Polished30%, Exalted8%, Ascension2%; no guaranteed drop or pity counter. <a href=\"zones.html\">Zone rewards</a>.</p>\n<h2 id=\"hunt-sockets\">Six armor locations for heroic augments</h2><p>Eligible Base and tiered head, arms, hands, chest, legs and feet armor gains one type-22 socket, preserving existing sockets. Zone augments add stats and heroic attributes; item level requirements still apply. At level 50, every two effective heroic INT from these socketed augments allows one more point of item Spell Damage, up to +30. Heroic WIS does the same for Healing Amount. With the current 750 cap, either can reach 780. Extra cap room only helps when you have enough of the actual bonus.</p>\n<h2 id=\"zone-forge\">Upgrade matching rewards</h2><p><code>#zoneforge</code> uses <strong>three Base copies</strong> for one Polished reward, then <strong>four Polished</strong> for one Exalted or <strong>four Exalted</strong> for one Ascension. Artisan Veyra’s reusable Reforging Box also upgrades four identical Polished or Exalted copies, including eligible ordinary tiered gear. The box also accepts <a href=\"item-upgrades.html#normal-items\">three identical eligible Normal/Base copies for Polished</a>; higher recipes stay at four. Read <a href=\"item-upgrades.html\">Item upgrades</a> for inputs, restrictions and the two distinct top-tier names.</p>\n<details class=\"guide-topic\" id=\"heroic-gear\"><summary>Heroic stats on Ascended equipment</summary><div class=\"topic-body\"><p>Ascended gear and Ascended epics add heroic stats on top of their improved base stats. This describes the existing equipment tiers; the new zone rewards have their own heroic stats at each quality.</p>\n</div></details><details class=\"guide-topic\" id=\"caster-gear\"><summary>Gear bonuses for casters and healers</summary><div class=\"topic-body\"><p>Eligible direct damage spells and procs add effective Spell Damage once. Each ordinary DoT tick adds half the effective bonus, rounded down, independent of duration. Healing Amount keeps percentage healing and its existing HoT distribution. Each item-bonus total has a 750 base cap; eligible Hunt augments can raise it to 780 at level 50 when enough actual bonus is equipped. Each heroic INT point adds 0.1% direct damage. Each heroic WIS point adds 0.1% direct healing. DoTs and HoTs do not receive this multiplier. The separate Bard area-DoT route keeps its behavior.</p>\n</div></details><details class=\"guide-topic\" id=\"stat-cap\"><summary>More room for core stats</summary><div class=\"topic-body\"><p>The normal core-stat cap is raised to 425, with heroic stat effects handled separately.</p>\n</div></details><details class=\"guide-topic\" id=\"summoned-gear\"><summary>Ascended summoned equipment</summary><div class=\"topic-body\"><p>Eligible summoned gear becomes Ascended when a matching version exists. The supported Paladin and Cleric summoned-hammer families have zero merchant resale value at every quality, including items you already own. Summoning does not bypass spell or item-level requirements.</p>\n</div></details><h2 id=\"bags\">More room in your bags</h2><p>Buy bags up to 40 slots, with base prices from 10 to 7,500 platinum. Merchant price adjustments and each bag’s capacity and contents restrictions still apply. Free trading does not reduce expensive bag purchase prices.</p>\n<details class=\"guide-topic\" id=\"merchant-payouts\"><summary>Better payouts for ordinary loot</summary><div class=\"topic-body\"><p>Boosted merchant payouts remain in place for ordinary loot. Formerly NO DROP items use the fixed one-platinum payout below instead of those price modifiers.</p>\n</div></details><details class=\"guide-topic\" id=\"fixed-resale\"><summary>One platinum for formerly NO DROP items</summary><div class=\"topic-body\"><p>Ordinary merchants and <code>#sellall</code> pay exactly 1 platinum per physical item from the eligible formerly NO DROP pool. Five stack units pay 5 platinum; a charged object pays 1 platinum total. Purchase prices have a one-platinum floor. Merchant previews can differ from actual payment. Zone-hunt rewards, dungeon rewards and the supported divine summoned-hammer families have no merchant resale value.</p>\n</div></details><h2 id=\"selling\">Bulk selling from the command or merchant window</h2><p>Use <code>#sellall</code> to sell eligible carried items without targeting a merchant, or use the merchant window’s <strong>Sell All</strong> button. Containers, food, drink, spell reagents and casting focus items are kept. Zero-value items, including zone rewards and the supported divine summoned hammers, are skipped. <strong class=\"inline\">Sales are immediate and can include valuable gear. Bank anything you want to keep first.</strong></p>\n<h2 id=\"winged-helmet\">Winged Helm of the Dawn</h2><p>A custom Paladin helmet with an installed appearance for visual Play. <strong class=\"inline\">Earn this helmet through Camil’s Vigil of the Dawn, now in.</strong></p>\n\n<h2 id=\"eligibility\">Wear gear for your whole build</h2><p>Ordinary equipment recognizes all held classes. Class-matching wearable items and augments allow all playable races; deity, level, slot, weapon and augment restrictions remain. See <a href=\"multiclass.html#equipment-access\">equipment eligibility</a>.</p><h2 id=\"dungeon-rewards\">Dungeon completion rewards</h2><p><a href=\"dungeon-modes.html\">Raid and Grind dungeons</a> have 24 shared reward designs and three exclusive Raid designs for each of the 21 released dungeons. Grind grants Normal; Raid grants Polished or Ascended. These permanent, tradeable, non-lore items have zero merchant resale and no existing forging recipe. Their bags have up to ten slots and 100% weight reduction.</p>\n\n<h2 id=\"click-cooldowns\">Item click reuse</h2><p>Items without an explicit shared reuse group keep their own cooldowns without locking unrelated abilities. Copies of the same item share reuse; explicitly grouped items still share their group. Existing saved waits keep their expiry. See <a href=\"combat.html#ability-cooldowns\">the cooldown update</a>.</p>\n<details class=\"guide-topic\" id=\"reviewed-ascended\"><summary>Ascended values</summary><div class=\"topic-body\"><p>Supported numeric fields on 131 Ascended items now follow inspected THJ Legendary references. These families use per-item values rather than one universal multiplier. Some values are lower than before; original effects and existing sockets remain.</p><table><caption>Selected Ascended reference values</caption><thead><tr><th>Item</th><th>Values</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Heavy Yttrium Chestplate</td><td>150 AC; 250 HP and mana; 40 Spell Damage and Healing Amount</td></tr><tr><td>Blood Cord</td><td>70 AC; 200 HP and mana; 40 STA and 10 heroic STA; 40 Spell Damage and Healing Amount</td></tr><tr><td>Talisman of Vah Kerrath</td><td>250 HP and mana; 8 to each heroic attribute; 30 Spell Damage and Healing Amount</td></tr></tbody></table></div></details><details class=\"guide-topic\" id=\"starter-bands\"><summary>Starter upgrades and dungeon progression</summary><div class=\"topic-body\"><p>starter families use smaller steps: Bronze chest armor has 6, 7, 8 and 9 AC across Normal, Polished, Exalted and Ascended. Bronze Long Sword has 4, 5, 6 and 7 damage at fixed delay 32. Cultural armor is excluded from this retuning. Comparable Normal dungeon rewards remain stronger.</p></div></details><details class=\"guide-topic\" id=\"earned-procs\"><summary>Earned melee and pet equipment</summary><div class=\"topic-body\"><p>Selected items gain sympathetic healing, combat procs or received-healing support. Healing, Runic and Hastened Fragments of Truth and Bloodfrenzy Core have earned boss routes; later-era bosses still require their normal access. Bloodfrenzy Core is a power-source item, while the original Bloodfrenzy remains a weapon. New sockets do not bypass augment compatibility.</p>\n</div></details><h2 id=\"class-armor-candidate\">Ascended class-armor quest rewards</h2><p>Crafted, Lambent, Darkforge, Ivy Etched and Totemic quests now grant existing Ascended versions of their 37 armor rewards. Substantial class-armor quests qualify even when repeatable; cheap/basic hand-ins stay excluded. Materials and quest requirements remain. Already-owned armor is not automatically converted. <a href=\"unreleased.html#quest-quality\">Scope and</a>.</p>\n\n<h2 id=\"chapterhouse-candidate\">The Vigil of the Dawn</h2><p>The Winged Helm of the Dawn is earned through Camil’s Vigil of the Dawn. Its existing stats and sockets remain unchanged. Chapterhouse also awards three miniboss items, six final Raid variants and a four-quality augment. <a href=\"camil-vigil.html\">Read the quest guide</a> and <a href=\"zone-chapterhouse.html\">reward catalog</a>.</p>\n<h2 id=\"quest-ingredients\">Quest ingredients and item quality</h2><p>Normal-item quest requirements accept Polished, Exalted and Ascended versions of the same item. Shakrn Meadowgreen in South Karana accepts an Aviak Charm of any ordinary quality plus two Star Rubies for Ascended Crafted Gauntlets. Ingredients are consumed; their quality does not upgrade the configured reward. Exact Normal inputs are used first when both are offered. Explicit quality requirements, reforging recipes and separate epic, hunt and dungeon catalogs keep their own rules.</p>\n<details class=\"guide-topic\" id=\"thj-behavior-candidate\"><summary>How ordinary item stats scale</summary><div class=\"topic-body\"><p>The update uses unmodified stock ProjectEQ as an approximation of standard EverQuest, then preserves the exact researched values where available. It changes 143,332 existing tier definitions across 47,809 eligible ordinary families. Normal items, the 209 starter families, custom Hunt/dungeon rewards, augment families and quest-only epics keep their existing treatment. Families that exceed stat limits are excluded for review.</p><table><thead><tr><th>Ascended field</th><th>Target from stock</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Positive AC, HP, mana, primary stats, resists, weapon damage and HP/mana regeneration</td><td>2×</td></tr><tr><td>Haste</td><td>1.5×, rounded</td></tr><tr><td>Spell Damage when stock has none</td><td>Higher of 2× INT or WIS</td></tr><tr><td>Healing Amount when stock has none</td><td>2× WIS</td></tr><tr><td>Accuracy when stock has none</td><td>Half DEX, rounded upward</td></tr><tr><td>New heroics</td><td>Quarter of the final matching stat, rounded; Ascended only</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Polished and Exalted receive one-third and two-thirds of the increase from Normal to Ascended. These intermediate formulas and extrapolation beyond the screenshots are Nightcap tuning choices. Attack and sparse utility fields use stock values unless an exact observed override applies. Existing effects, sockets, delays, equip rules, loot routes and owned items are preserved.</p>\n\n</div></details><span id=\"loot-finder-preview\"></span><span id=\"classic-robes\"></span><h2 id=\"ashen-compact\">The Ashen Compact</h2><p><a href=\"ashen-compact.html\">The Ashen Compact</a> is an installed level-50 Shadow Knight helmet campaign in a custom Kael expedition.</p><p>The Warhelm of the Ashen Compact uses the Paladin helm budget with INT replacing WIS. It requires a held Shadow Knight class. Its new enclosed Classic appearance requires the paired client update.</p>\n<h2 id=\"player-bazaar\">Persistent player listings</h2><p> Its supported permanent items and stacks remain listed while the seller is offline. It has stricter posting requirements than direct player trading, including empty bags and exactly recoverable saved item data. <a href=\"tunnel.html#player-bazaar\">Market instructions and restrictions</a>.</p>\n<h2 id=\"paladin-weapon-grip\">Paladin weapon grips</h2><p><strong>Paired October28 update:</strong> fully exit EQ and use launcher Play to install release2026102801. It repairs the stale client definition that could leave SoulFire two-handed after a 1HS message.</p><p>The assessed stats are. Ascended SoulFire uses 26/30 in 1HS or 46/45 in 2HS with Accuracy 10. Ascended Avenger uses 30/30 or 66/44 with Accuracy 15. Ascended Defender uses 36/30 or 72/40 with Accuracy 25. Avenger adds 1 point and Defender adds 3 points of shield block with an eligible shield in 1HS. Defender also gains improved healing and heroic wisdom, with its proc available at level 45. Grip changes preserve augments and saved charges. The one-handed grip stays primary-only. Shield abilities and augments can affect which grip deals more damage.</p><p>The SoulFire, Fiery Avenger and Fiery Defender quests award their Ascended versions directly. No extra essence or platinum is required for Defender. Owners of an original Defender can use the free <a href=\"ascension.html\">Epic Forgemaster exchange</a>, preserving its grip and customizations. There is no automatic inventory conversion. Meet each quest's faction and ingredient requirements.</p><p>Change grip out of combat and casting. Remove the shield before returning an equipped weapon to 2HS; augments must support the destination type. SoulFire's heal click is replaced by the grip toggle. Return to 2HS before reforging eligible copies. The grip is saved per item, including Bazaar transfers; generic links and type filters describe the base 2HS definition.</p>\n<h2 id=\"augment-description-correction\">Equipped bonuses in Inventory Stats</h2><p>Open <strong>Inventory → Stats</strong> to see your current server-calculated equipped bonuses and caps. Values update automatically while the tab is open. Shield Block and the relative Dodge modifier have their own rows. Scroll down for item spell-haste and mana-preservation potential and worn Faerune. Focus values are the best equipped item potential before spell limits; they are not a promise for every cast. The separate Shielding row remains melee damage reduction. Damage/healing caps include earned headroom. Bagged and training items give no bonus.</p><p>After fully exiting EverQuest, use launcher Play to install signed update2026110604 (client0.13.4). A missing or stale server reply shows “--”. <code>#augstats</code> remains a diagnostic fallback.</p><p>Shield Block shows one total including equipped augment bonuses. The strongest augment shield-block bonus applies; two +1% copies still give +1%. Shielding remains a separate damage-reduction stat.</p><h2 id=\"last-lantern\">Last Lantern campaign armor</h2><p>Earn eight personal armor pieces over the <a href=\"adventure-journal.html\">level 20–50 Adventure Journal</a>, with legal woven, leather, chain or plate fits and earned refits. <a href=\"last-lantern-equipment.html\">Exact stats and chapters</a>.; harder endgame loot remains worthwhile.</p>\n<h2 id=\"augment-icon-candidate\">Stat augments and equipment icons</h2><p>Ordinary stat augments keep the equipment's own icon and appearance. Genuine cosmetic ornaments still change appearance. If an older item displays an augment icon, report the item name and slot to the owner; do not destroy augments as a workaround.</p>\n<h2 id=\"inventory-combat-summary\">Combat stats and heroic attributes in Inventory</h2>\n<p>The main <strong>Inventory</strong> tab shows AC, MIT, AVD, ATK, DMG and HEAL above your attributes. MIT is the mitigation AC rating used by the server. AVD is the server defense rating used for the hit check, not the item Avoidance bonus or a percentage chance to dodge. AC remains the conventional client display. ATK is your attack rating; DMG and HEAL are Spell Damage and Healing Amount bonuses, not damage or healing per cast.</p>\n<p>Each attribute has a <strong>green current value</strong>, a <strong>white /cap</strong> and a <strong>yellow/gold signed heroic total</strong>. The cap is the actual server cap, including heroic allowance. Heroics are already included in the current value and cap: do not add the yellow number again. No heroic bonus displays as <strong>+0</strong>. Missing or stale server totals show <strong>--</strong> while refreshing.</p>\n<p>Fully exit EverQuest and use normal launcher <strong>Play</strong> to install the latest client update. The main Inventory tab has no scrollbars. The wider information column keeps the normal font readable. The separate Stats tab keeps equipped secondary bonuses, focus potential and the single Shield Block total.</p><p><a href=\"classic-raid-augments.html\">Classic raid augments</a> drop from 25 named bosses. Choose one level-50 chest trophy for damage, healing, defense or resource recovery.</p><h2 id=\"stock-sympathetic\">Classic sympathetic clicks</h2><p>Any class can use these two Ascended items. Only the Ascended copies grant the buffs. You can also make them with the ordinary <a href=\"item-upgrades.html#normal-items\">Reforging Box recipes</a>.</p><ol><li>Equip the item.</li><li>Right-click it to start the two-second cast.</li><li>After the cast, put your usual gear back on.</li></ol><p>Both buffs can stay active together. Use the same item again to refresh its buff.</p><ul><li><strong>Sympathetic Strike I.</strong> A lava elemental in Solusek’s Eye drops the <a href=\"loot-finder.html?item=610338\">Runed Lava Pendant (Ascended)</a>. Cast a single-target direct damage spell from a spell gem. The base mana cost must be at least 10 before mana preservation. If the spell lands fully, the target takes one extra hit. An eligible lifetap deals extra damage without increasing its healing.</li><li><strong>Sympathetic Healing I.</strong> A frenzied ghoul in Lower Guk drops the <a href=\"loot-finder.html?item=610150\">Moonstone Ring (Ascended)</a>. The ring keeps Extended Range II. Cast a single-target direct heal from a spell gem. The spell must have a base mana cost above zero. The same target receives one extra heal. If a worn sympathetic focus delivers a direct heal on this cast, the worn effect takes precedence.</li></ul><p>Each bonus equals 5% of the largest eligible hit or heal from the cast. Round down to a maximum of 48. A 40-point heal gives 2 extra before overheal. A 960-point hit gives 48 extra before target protections.</p><p>Area spells, spells with a duration and partial resists cannot activate either buff. Pet casts, item clicks and triggered casts also give no bonus.</p><h2 id=\"stock-worn-atk\">Worn ATK on stock gear</h2><p>The 135 families below gain ATK as they improve in quality. The item window shows its full value. If your character is below an item’s recommended level, the server reduces its contribution before adding it to your worn ATK. The base worn cap is 250. Applicable item, spell and AA bonuses can raise the cap.</p><p>For example, an Ascended Armguard of Shadows lists 53 ATK. It contributes up to 44 at level 50 and 53 at its recommended level of 60. If your other gear already reaches the cap, equipping more worn ATK adds zero. The Inventory ATK rating also includes skills, STR and other bonuses.</p><details><summary>Compare all 135 families by quality</summary><div class=\"table-scroll\"><table><thead><tr><th>Equipment</th><th>Normal</th><th>Polished</th><th>Exalted</th><th>Ascended</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Abalone Engraved Tribal Mask</td><td>0</td><td>3</td><td>7</td><td>10</td></tr><tr><td>Akkirus' Mask of Warfare</td><td>0</td><td>3</td><td>7</td><td>10</td></tr><tr><td>Armguard of Shadows</td><td>50</td><td>51</td><td>52</td><td>53</td></tr><tr><td>Askr's Thunderous Boots</td><td>20</td><td>21</td><td>23</td><td>24</td></tr><tr><td>Band of Swirling Air</td><td>0</td><td>5</td><td>10</td><td>15</td></tr><tr><td>Belt of Mastery</td><td>10</td><td>11</td><td>11</td><td>12</td></tr><tr><td>Belt of Temporal Bindings</td><td>0</td><td>7</td><td>13</td><td>20</td></tr><tr><td>Belt of Tidal Energy</td><td>0</td><td>2</td><td>3</td><td>5</td></tr><tr><td>Black Enchanted Amulet</td><td>0</td><td>2</td><td>3</td><td>5</td></tr><tr><td>Blazing Bracers of Discovery</td><td>10</td><td>11</td><td>11</td><td>12</td></tr><tr><td>Boots of the Warmaster</td><td>20</td><td>21</td><td>23</td><td>24</td></tr><tr><td>Bow of the Tempest</td><td>30</td><td>33</td><td>35</td><td>38</td></tr><tr><td>Bracelet of Darkness</td><td>0</td><td>3</td><td>7</td><td>10</td></tr><tr><td>Bracer of Black Blood</td><td>20</td><td>21</td><td>22</td><t