-  "body": "<h2 id=\"titles-automatic-suffix\">November 14: automatic titles and matching suffixes</h2><p>Titles now unlock automatically when earned, with a chat message and a new-title alert. Every prefix also unlocks a matching suffix through the same achievement. Existing awards gain their matching suffix without another grind. Login and zoning automatically check recorded goals. <code>#titles</code> remains an optional progress list. <a href=\"titles.html\">Title names and requirements</a>.</p><h2 id=\"titles-active\">November 14: earned titles available</h2><p>The <a href=\"titles.html\">77 cosmetic titles</a> and <code>#titles</code> are available. Open the Titles window to check existing completion and skill goals. New slayer totals start now. Nagafen earns Flamebreaker; defeating both Nagafen and Vox earns Dragonslayer. Newly earned titles notify you and never replace your selected title.</p><h2 id=\"backstab-weapons\">November 13 · Backstab weapons</h2><p>Backstab now uses the stronger qualifying weapon in either hand. See <a href=\"combat.html#backstab-weapons\">how Backstab chooses your weapon</a>.</p><h2 id=\"bow-damage\">November 13 · Bow damage</h2><p>Heroic Dexterity now increases damage from ordinary bow shots. See the <a href=\"combat.html#bow-damage\">bow damage table and Archery Mastery ranks</a>.</p><h2 id=\"stock-sympathetic\">November 13 · Classic sympathetic clicks</h2><p>The Ascended Runed Lava Pendant now grants Sympathetic Strike I. The Ascended Moonstone Ring grants Sympathetic Healing I. Exit EverQuest. Select Play in the Nightcap launcher to get the new spell descriptions. See <a href=\"equipment.html#stock-sympathetic\">item sources, eligible spells and bonus amounts</a>.</p><h2 id=\"wiki-simple-20261113\">November 13: wiki layout</h2><p>The wiki has a simpler layout, shorter guides and direct topic links.</p><h2 id=\"stock-worn-atk\">November 13 · Stock equipment ATK</h2><p>Polished, Exalted and Ascended versions of 135 stock families now use updated worn ATK. <a href=\"equipment.html#stock-worn-atk\">See all item values and how the cap works</a> </p><h2 id=\"classic-raid-augments\">November 12 · Classic raid boss augments</h2><p>Classic raid augments drop from 25 named bosses. <a href=\"classic-raid-augments.html\">Classic raid augments</a> </p><h2 id=\"inventory-combat-summary\">November 12: Inventory combat stats, caps and heroics</h2><p>Signed client 2026111202 with proxy 0.13.6 adds the combat summary and current/cap/heroic attributes to the main Inventory tab. <a href=\"equipment.html#inventory-combat-summary\">Instructions</a> </p>\n<h2 id=\"dot-initial-damage-20261112\">November 12: DoT initial damage removed</h2><p>Player DoTs no longer deal their separate cast-time damage hit. <a href=\"combat.html#dot-initial-damage\">Timing details</a> </p>\n<h2 id=\"imitate-death\">November 12: Imitate Death without cooldown</h2><p>Removed Imitate Death's ability cooldown and retired its old saved wait. <a href=\"combat.html#imitate-death\">Hotkey instructions and limits</a> </p>\n<h2 id=\"quick-buff-hotkey-fix-20261112\">November 12: Quick Buff hotkey creation fixed</h2><p>Fixed the disabled Make Hotkey button for players who own Quick Buff. <a href=\"combat.html#quick-buff-hotkey-ready\">Hotkey instructions</a> </p>\n<h2 id=\"quick-buff-20261112\">November 12: Quick Buff hotkey</h2><p>Quick Buff replaces passive buff haste with an activated hotkey that immediately casts eligible memorized buffs for 50% maximum mana with no reuse delay. <a href=\"combat.html#quick-buff-hotkey\">Hotkey instructions</a> </p>\n<h2 id=\"last-lantern-20261107\">November7: The Last Lantern</h2><p>The Adventure Journal continues to level 50. Complete eight private memories, choose from five oath paths and earn an eight-piece armor outfit. <a href=\"adventure-journal.html\">Start, chapters and rewards</a> </p>\n<h2 id=\"advanced-loot-repair-20261107\">November 7: Advanced Loot client repair</h2><p>Client 2026110605 repairs automatic opening after closing Filters and visibility after a skin reload, including new loot beyond the first page. <a href=\"advanced-loot.html#row-controls\">Controls and update instructions</a> </p>\n<span id=\"keeper-readiness-20261106\"></span><p>Raid and Grind entry now accepts the current expedition augment release.</p><h2 id=\"shield-block-total\">November6: one Shield Block total</h2><p>Update2026110604 keeps a single Shield Block row, including equipped augment bonuses, and removes the redundant augment-only breakdown.</p>\n<h2 id=\"stats-font\">November6: Stats font and Hunt label</h2><p>Update2026110603 matches the added Stats rows to the normal font and row height.</p>\n<h2 id=\"character-stats-window\">November6: automatic equipped Stats</h2><p>Signed client0.13.4/update2026110602 adds Shield Block, Hunt contribution, relative Dodge, item focus potential and worn Faerune to Inventory Stats. <a href=\"equipment.html#augment-description-correction\">How to check your stats</a> </p>\n<h2 id=\"augment-audit-20261106\">November6: zone augments and exotic icons</h2><p>Augments can drop from any unowned killable NPC in enabled zones, including guards, named enemies, killable merchants and scripted adds. <a href=\"augment-audit.html\">Full list and limits</a> </p><h2 id=\"hunt-rates-20261101\">November 1: zone augments drop three times as often - live</h2><p>Zone Hunt augments now drop at 1.5% per eligible kill (was 0.5%), about one per 67 kills. <a href=\"zone-hunt.html#drops\">How drops work</a> </p><h2 id=\"ssf-20261101\">November 1: solo self-found mode -</h2><p>New level-1 characters can swear a permanent solo self-found oath at the Ancient Chronicler. <a href=\"multiclass.html#solo-self-found\">How it works</a> </p><h2 id=\"hate-density-20261030\">October 30: Plane of Hate density -</h2><p> <a href=\"dungeon-modes.html#hate-layout-preview\">Hate modes and landmarks</a> </p>\n<h2 id=\"public-cazic-20261030\">October 30 — public Classic Cazic-Thule restored</h2><p>Restored 188 Classic encounter points in open-world Cazic-Thule, which previously had no eligible combat population under Classic.</p><h2 id=\"recall-labels-20261030\">October 30: Commonlands recall labels corrected</h2><p class=\"notice\">Recall labels corrected (October 30): Client release 2026103001 restores Ancient Attunement’s name, Nightcap Recall’s hotbutton label and the recall description.</p>\n<details class=\"change-entry\" open><summary>October28: Bazaar posting and readable controls</summary><div class=\"change-body\"><p>Client update2026102803 accepts valid whole-platinum digits in both text formats, reports unreadable input, and enlarges seller text with light colors.</p></div></details><details class=\"change-entry\" open><summary>October 26: Bazaar seller panel and Paladin grips</summary><div class=\"change-body\"><h2 id=\"bazaar-panel-candidate\">Sell / My Listings controls</h2><p>Client update 2026102601 adds the Sell / My Listings tab for posting, cancelling owned listings and collecting offline proceeds. <a href=\"tunnel.html#bazaar-seller-panel\">Panel instructions</a> </p></div></details><h2 id=\"commonlands-bazaar-20261026\">October 26: Commonlands player bazaar</h2><p>Persistent player listings, offline seller proceeds and search/purchase routing are installed in public East Commonlands. <a href=\"tunnel.html#player-bazaar\">Market instructions and restrictions</a> </p>\n<h2 id=\"october24-coordinated\">October 24 — High Keep rescue, Ashen Compact and aggro corrections</h2><p>New High Keep Raid runs now rescue Osargen.</p>\n<h2 id=\"ashen-compact-everfrost\">October 24 — Ashen Compact entrance</h2><p>Its frostbound crossing and return connect to custom Kael. <a href=\"ashen-compact.html\">Shadow Knight campaign</a> </p><h2 id=\"rogue-tome-learning\">October 24 - Multiclass tome learning repaired</h2><p>Eligible tomes can now be learned through any held class, fixing secondary and third-class Rogue learning. <a href=\"multiclass.html#learning-tomes\">learning combat disciplines</a> </p><h2 id=\"custom-feature-directory\">October 24 — Custom content on Features</h2><p>Features now groups Raid &amp; Grind dungeons, helmet quests, Zone Hunt, epic reforging, class armor, crafting, exploration and custom character systems. <a href=\"features.html\">Features</a> </p><p>Current instructions live in Guides. <a href=\"all-pages.html\">Guides</a> </p><details class=\"change-entry\" id=\"wiki-clarity\" open><summary>October 24, 2026 · A clearer wiki</summary><div class=\"change-body\"><p>Features now highlights the major differences from standard EQ.</p></div></details><details class=\"change-entry\" id=\"hole-entrance\"><summary>October 24 · The Hole entrance</summary><div class=\"change-body\"><p class=\"notice\">— keyless Hole entrance: The Hole Key and lock-picking requirement have been removed from the entrance rock in Paineel at /loc 568,-896,-96.</p>\n</div></details><details class=\"change-entry\" id=\"aa-level-progression\"><summary>October 23: two AA per level and level-1 AA controls</summary><div class=\"change-body\"><p>The paired update is.</p>\n</div></details><details class=\"change-entry\" id=\"chapterhouse-candidate\"><summary>October 23 · The Vigil of the Dawn</summary><div class=\"change-body\"><p>October 23: Camil’s Chapterhouse quest, level-50–53 encounters, custom rewards, Ember augment, waypoint and Keeper are deployed. <a href=\"camil-vigil.html\">Read the quest guide</a> <a href=\"zone-chapterhouse.html\">reward catalog</a> </p>\n</div></details><details class=\"change-entry\" id=\"loot-finder-preview\"><summary>October 22: production loot finder</summary><div class=\"change-body\"><p>The Loot finder supports class, slot, quality, level and zone filters. Item links show enemy sources, locations and drop chances. <a href=\"loot-finder.html\">class and era loot finder</a> </p><p class=\"notice\" id=\"hate-commonlands-candidate\">— Hate Keeper in Commonlands: Find the Plane of Hate Keeper in East Commonlands at /loc -1570,-346,3, between Mirielle and Khalure in the travel area.</p>\n</div></details><details class=\"change-entry\" id=\"build-lab\"><summary>Build Lab — October 22</summary><div class=\"change-body\"><p>The Build Lab compares two saved builds, supported spell benefits, Hunt item stat differences and editable ability priorities. <a href=\"build-lab.html\">Build Lab</a> </p>\n</div></details><details class=\"change-entry\" id=\"interactive-handbook\"><summary>October 22 — Your interactive field guide</summary><div class=\"change-body\"><p>The wiki has a new lantern-lit design with four adventure paths, instant quick search, saved guides, light and dark reading modes, and a reading-progress bar. <a href=\"about.html#navigation\">Learn the shortcuts and field notes →</a> </p><p class=\"notice\">The Classic raid rewards give every dungeon three exclusive designs. <a href=\"dungeon-modes.html#unique-rewards\">Classic raid rewards</a> </p>\n</div></details><details class=\"change-entry\" id=\"classic-dungeons-candidate\"><summary>October 22 — every Classic dungeon and unique rewards live</summary><div class=\"change-body\"><p class=\"notice\">Every Classic dungeon coverage adds the same Raid/Grind choices in 21 combat dungeon zones, including Fear, Hate and Sky. <a href=\"dungeon-modes.html#classic-candidate\">Every Classic dungeon coverage</a> </p>\n<p>The paired release also repairs stale dungeon item checks behind the reported Keeper error and installs durable Sky key services.</p>\n</div></details><details class=\"change-entry\" id=\"quest-ingredients-20261022\"><summary>October 22 - quest ingredient fix live for Play</summary><div class=\"change-body\"><p>Polished, Exalted and Ascended ingredients can satisfy Normal quest requirements, including Aviak Charm for Crafted Gauntlets. <a href=\"equipment.html#quest-ingredients\">Scope and limits</a> </p>\n</div></details><details class=\"change-entry\" id=\"class-armor-candidate\"><summary>October 22 — Ascended class-armor quest rewards</summary><div class=\"change-body\"><p>Crafted, Lambent, Darkforge, Ivy Etched and Totemic quests now grant 37 Ascended armor rewards. <a href=\"unreleased.html#quest-quality\">Reward guide</a> </p>\n</div></details><details class=\"change-entry\" id=\"crystal-markers\"><summary>October 22 · Waypoint crystals</summary><div class=\"change-body\"><p>Waypoints now have a glowing crystal with the existing a waypoint label.</p>\n</div></details><details class=\"change-entry\" id=\"classic-robes-20261022\"><summary>October 22 — robe waist correction in</summary><div class=\"change-body\"><p>Game update 2026102204 repairs the waist binding after the earlier 2026102203 repair failed, covering all seven added Classic robe races and both genders. <a href=\"equipment.html#classic-robes\">Read the scope</a> </p>\n</div></details><details class=\"change-entry\" id=\"keeper-visibility-20261022\"><summary>October 22 — Dungeon Keeper placement</summary><div class=\"change-body\"><p>The correction now separates Keepers from overlapping waypoints in Befallen, Unrest, Najena, Permafrost and Nagafen’s Lair. <a href=\"dungeon-modes.html\">All seven Keeper locations</a> </p>\n<p class=\"notice\">Level-scaled AA: Earn two AA per level while leveling. <a href=\"multiclass.html#passive-abilities\">AA progression and examples</a> </p></div></details><details class=\"change-entry\" id=\"aa-million-xp\"><summary>October 21: slower AA earning and XP boost retirement</summary><div class=\"change-body\"><p>The October 21 release used 1,000,000 AA experience per point with 10% passive earning; the October 23 level-scaled update supersedes that earning model.</p>\n</div></details><details class=\"change-entry\" id=\"thj-behavior-candidate\"><summary>October 19 · THJ behavior and stock gear</summary><div class=\"change-body\"><p>The custom AA, spell focus and stock-derived gear update is. <a href=\"unreleased.html#thj-behavior-candidate\">behavior details and open Play limits</a> </p>\n</div></details><details class=\"change-entry\" id=\"all-class-aa-20261019\"><summary>October 19: all-class AA update</summary><div class=\"change-body\"><p class=\"notice\">Live AA Play: All 16 classes have more earned AA options: 75 newly available lines, 111 expanded lines and Druid access to Healing Boon. <a href=\"multiclass.html#all-class-aa\">Read the AA update</a> </p>\n<p class=\"notice\">Launch repair published: Game update 2026101901 corrects the client catalog mismatch that blocked Play after the previous update.</p>\n</div></details><details class=\"change-entry\" id=\"thj-release\"><summary>October 18: item, spell, pet and melee release</summary><div class=\"change-body\"><p>Selected Ascended items now use THJ values.</p><p>Permanent-pet equipment now has pages. The update also changes pet and melee AAs, Rabid Bear effects and shared stat limits. </p>\n<h2>October 18 - More ordinary quality loot</h2><p>Polished, Exalted and Ascended now have 20%, 5% and 1% chances per eligible ordinary equipment/bag drop.</p></div></details><details class=\"change-entry\" id=\"reforge-colors\"><summary>October 18, 2026: built-in item colors</summary><div class=\"change-body\"><p>The Reforging Box and zone forging now accept an item's built-in color. <a href=\"item-upgrades.html#requirements\">Reforging Box</a> <a href=\"zone-hunt.html#forging\">zone forging</a> </p>\n</div></details><details class=\"change-entry\" id=\"october-18-cooldowns\"><summary>October 18, 2026: separate ability cooldowns</summary><div class=\"change-body\"><p>Activated AA families now have independent cooldowns, including Rampage and Purify Body. <a href=\"combat.html#ability-cooldowns\">Activated AA families now have independent cooldowns</a> <a href=\"unreleased.html#cooldown-identities\">generic skill and content-defined groups</a> </p>\n</div></details><details class=\"change-entry\" id=\"october-18\"><summary>October 18, 2026: Classic travel file repair</summary><div class=\"change-body\"><p>Signed game update 2026101801 adds automatic missing/corrupt terrain and object archive repair for 17 Classic travel destinations, including West Commonlands, Misty Thicket and Toxxulia.</p>\n</div></details><details class=\"change-entry\" id=\"october-17\"><summary>October 17, 2026: progression, combat and crafting</summary><div class=\"change-body\"><ul><li>The optional <a href=\"multiclass.html#recommended-aa\">Recommended AA filter</a> provides an early survival, sustain and damage shortlist across held classes.</li><li>Passive AA is now 10%, preserving full leveling EXP, earned points and 4,000 AA XP per point.</li><li><a href=\"combat.html#monk-cooldowns\">Six basic Monk attacks</a> have separate reuse. <a href=\"combat.html#cooldown-corrections\">Cooldown duration repairs</a> address excessive and restarted timers; other shared identities remain under investigation.</li><li><a href=\"combat.html#death-exp\">Normal death costs no EXP or levels</a>; prior losses are not refunded.</li><li><a href=\"tradeskills.html#stack-limits\">Stackable items support at least 100</a>, retaining larger limits.</li><li>The <a href=\"item-upgrades.html#normal-items\">Reforging Box accepts three identical eligible Normal/Base copies</a> for Polished. Higher recipes still cost four.</li><li>Idle zones can unload without ending their workers and triggering a whole-game restart.</li><li>Update through launcher Play for the matched client.</li></ul>\n</div></details><details class=\"change-entry\" id=\"october-16\"><summary>October 16, 2026</summary><div class=\"change-body\"><ul><li>The <a href=\"dungeon-modes.html#required-bosses\">dungeon guide now lists every required boss</a> and explains boss-stage notices, full-clear credit and Keeper Status when task objectives are blank.</li><li><a href=\"dungeon-modes.html\">Raid and Grind dungeons</a> are deployed with personal boss checklists, shared rewards and exclusive Raid drops.</li><li><a href=\"features.html\">Features</a> now gathers the major departures from Classic.</li><li><a href=\"multiclass.html#equipment-access\">Equipment eligibility</a> recognizes held classes and permits playable races when the class matches; remaining restrictions still apply.</li><li><a href=\"combat.html#buffs\">Temporary AA buffs</a> keep their timers; ordinary blessings remain lasting.</li><li><a href=\"tunnel.html#banking\">Mira Coinwell</a> provides tunnel banking. Haldra stocks Leather Padding.</li><li>The wiki’s guides, commands and generated reward pages have been together against current release evidence.</li></ul>\n</div></details><details class=\"change-entry\" id=\"october-13\"><summary>October 13, 2026</summary><div class=\"change-body\"><ul><li><a href=\"multiclass.html#passive-abilities\">Passive AA changed from 40% to 20%</a>, preserving full normal XP and 4,000 AA XP per point.</li><li><a href=\"multiclass.html#alternate-abilities\">All allowed AA ranks open at level 1</a>; points, eligibility and prerequisite ranks remain.</li><li><a href=\"tradeskills.html\">Stacked tradeskill ingredients and Craft All</a> are deployed.</li><li>The tunnel workshop layout is more spacious; the <a href=\"waypoints.html\">Unrest waypoint</a> moved beside its entrance Keeper.</li><li>Supported divine summoned-hammer families have <a href=\"equipment.html#summoned-gear\">zero resale value</a>.</li><li>The reported multiclass training/offhand issue and merchant Sell All button issue were confirmed resolved.</li></ul>\n</div></details><details class=\"change-entry\" id=\"october-12\"><summary>October 11–12, 2026</summary><div class=\"change-body\"><ul><li><a href=\"item-upgrades.html\">Reusable four-copy upgrades</a> are available from Artisan Veyra; higher #zoneforge steps now use four copies.</li><li><a href=\"equipment.html#free-trade\">LORE restrictions are disabled</a>. Food and drink requirements were removed.</li><li><a href=\"multiclass.html#spell-access\">Early scribing</a> allows eligible scrolls into the spellbook before their casting level.</li><li><a href=\"equipment.html#selling\">Sell All protects food, drink, reagents and casting focus items</a>.</li><li>The launcher uses personal access codes and shows <a href=\"launcher.html#patch-notes\">patch summaries</a>.</li><li>Waypoint portals and floating-eye Instance Keepers received visual corrections. The reported pet-summon crash was confirmed resolved.</li></ul>\n</div></details><details class=\"change-entry\" id=\"october-9\"><summary>October 9, 2026</summary><div class=\"change-body\"><ul><li><a href=\"zones.html\">48 Classic reward zones</a>, <a href=\"items.html\">384 reward variants</a>, type-22 augments and zone forging launched.</li><li>Passive AA increased to 40% at that time; the October 13 reduction above supersedes that rate.</li><li><a href=\"advanced-loot.html#row-controls\">Always Loot / Never Loot controls</a>, effective Spell Damage on <a href=\"combat.html#throw-stone\">Throw Stone</a>, and kept spell gems after normal death were added.</li></ul><p>See In development for candidates. <a href=\"unreleased.html\">More guides</a> </p>\n\n</div></details><h2 id=\"earlier-guide-notices\">Earlier release detail</h2><p>Notices previously repeated across guides are kept below for their original context.</p><details class=\"change-entry\"><summary>Ascension quest: earlier update details</summary><div class=\"change-body\"><h2 id=\"ascension--thj-behavior-candidate\">THJ behavior and stock gear</h2><p>The custom AA, spell focus and stock-derived gear update is. <a href=\"unreleased.html#thj-behavior-candidate\">behavior details and open Play limits</a> </p>\n</div></details><details class=\"change-entry\"><summary>Combat, buffs &amp; recovery: earlier update details</summary><div class=\"change-body\"><p class=\"notice\">Full gear, AA and pet effects are not automatically modeled. <a href=\"build-lab.html\">Try the Build Lab</a> </p>\n<h2 id=\"combat--thj-behavior-candidate\">THJ behavior and stock gear</h2><p>The custom AA, spell focus and stock-derived gear update is. <a href=\"unreleased.html#thj-behavior-candidate\">behavior details and open Play limits</a> </p><p>The update makes Improved Damage, Improved Healing, Mana Preservation, Reagent Conservation and Hate Adjustment use their strongest endpoints.</p>\n<p class=\"notice\">Live AA Play: All 16 classes have more earned AA options: 75 newly available lines, 111 expanded lines and Druid access to Healing Boon. <a href=\"multiclass.html#all-class-aa\">Read the AA update</a> </p>\n<p class=\"notice\">Direct Spell Damage, ordinary DoT ticks, heroic INT/WIS, pet healing and held-class melee effects have changed.</p>\n<h2 id=\"combat--cooldown-corrections\">Cooldown duration repairs</h2><p>Reuse reductions no longer create extremely long lockouts on item clicks, Mend, Bash, Frenzy and linked spells.</p>\n<h2 id=\"combat--blessing-repair\">Blessing effects that survive reconnects</h2><p>Repairs restore saved buff effects after login and stop permanent blessings expiring on the next tick.</p>\n</div></details><details class=\"change-entry\"><summary>Raid &amp; Grind dungeons: earlier update details</summary><div class=\"change-body\"><h2 id=\"dungeon-modes--hole-entrance\">The Hole entrance</h2><p class=\"notice\">— keyless Hole entrance: The Hole Key and lock-picking requirement have been removed from the entrance rock in Paineel at /loc 568,-896,-96.</p>\n<p class=\"notice\" id=\"dungeon-modes--hate-commonlands-candidate\">— Hate Keeper in Commonlands: Find the Plane of Hate Keeper in East Commonlands at /loc -1570,-346,3, between Mirielle and Khalure in the travel area.</p>\n<p class=\"notice\">Keepers offer Raid, Grind, Enter, Join, Status, Claim Rewards and Reset in 21 Classic dungeons. These include Fear, Hate and Sky. </p>\n<h2 id=\"dungeon-modes--classic-candidate\">Every Classic dungeon</h2><p>Added zones: blackburrow, crushbone, runnyeye, soldunga, guktop, gukbottom, mistmoore, kedge, paw, hole, qcat, fearplane, hateplane, airplane.</p><p>Added Raid final bosses receive three dungeon-specific exclusive designs in Polished and Ascended versions.</p>\n<p class=\"notice\">Keeper placement: The overlapping Keepers in Befallen, Unrest, Najena, Permafrost and Nagafen’s Lair now have positions 15 units from their waypoints.</p><table><thead><tr><th>Dungeon</th><th>Keeper /loc</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Befallen</td><td><code>-67,35,3.1</code></td></tr><tr><td>Unrest</td><td><code>-38,67,3.1</code></td></tr><tr><td>Najena</td><td><code>-61,858,4.1</code></td></tr><tr><td>Permafrost</td><td><code>-121,46,2.1</code></td></tr><tr><td>Nagafen’s Lair</td><td><code>-424,-248,-108</code></td></tr><tr><td>High Keep (unchanged)</td><td><code>-16,88,4</code></td></tr><tr><td>Cazic-Thule (unchanged)</td><td><code>71,-74,4</code></td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p class=\"notice\">Selected dungeon equipment budgets are raised so comparable Normal rewards exceed Ascended starter gear.</p>\n<p class=\"notice\">Raid and Grind dungeon modes are available from all 21 dungeon Keepers. <a href=\"dungeon-modes.html\">Raid and Grind dungeon modes</a> </p><p>Raid and Grind choices are available in all 21 Classic combat dungeons listed here, including Fear, Hate and Sky.</p>\n<h2 id=\"dungeon-modes--unique-rewards\">Unique Classic raid rewards</h2><p class=\"notice\">The Classic raid rewards give every dungeon three exclusive designs. <a href=\"dungeon-modes.html#unique-rewards\">Classic raid rewards</a> </p><p>New recommended levels follow each dungeon’s equipment band.</p><p>New numeric power stays within the existing band, slot and quality budgets.</p><table><thead><tr><th>Dungeon / band</th><th>Exclusive designs</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>blackburrow / 20</td><td>Elgnub's Burrowfang<br>Blackburrow Packwarden Mantle<br>Brewer's Amber Seal</td></tr><tr><td>crushbone / 20</td><td>Crush's Broken Scepter<br>Ambassador's Ashen Veil<br>Liberator of the Pens</td></tr><tr><td>runnyeye / 30</td><td>Pickclaw Tunnelbreaker<br>Evil Eye Witness<br>Crown of the Pickclaw Court</td></tr><tr><td>soldunga / 40</td><td>Goblin King's Cinderstaff<br>Firebloom Forgegrips<br>Embervault Reliquary</td></tr><tr><td>guktop / 30</td><td>Shinlord's Oathblade<br>Heart of the Living Guk<br>Reedwoven Watcher Boots</td></tr><tr><td>gukbottom / 50</td><td>Ghoul Lord's Last Decree<br>Pall of the Silent Court<br>Seal of Released Souls</td></tr><tr><td>mistmoore / 40</td><td>Xicotl's Midnight Talon<br>Mistmoore Bloodless Gorget<br>Echo of the Unfinished Waltz</td></tr><tr><td>kedge / 50</td><td>Phinigel's Tidebound Trident<br>Pearl of the Drowned Chorus<br>Kedge Deepcurrent Robe</td></tr><tr><td>paw / 40</td><td>Ishva's Splitpaw Knuckles<br>Splitpaw Spiritcord<br>Denfather Stoneguard</td></tr><tr><td>hole / 50</td><td>Wretched Stonecleaver<br>Pael Sealed Memory<br>Earthbound Oathplate</td></tr><tr><td>qcat / 20</td><td>Omorb's Sluicefang<br>Catacomb Vigil Lantern<br>Qeynos Underway Satchel</td></tr><tr><td>fearplane / 50</td><td>Spine of the Faceless<br>Visage of Unbroken Will<br>Dreadhusk of the Last Stand</td></tr><tr><td>hateplane / 50</td><td>Innoruuk's Severed Covenant<br>Maestro's Unfinished Requiem<br>Seal of the First Betrayal</td></tr><tr><td>airplane / 50</td><td>Veeshan's Unwritten Horizon<br>Mantle of the First Brood<br>Astrolabe of the Eighth Island</td></tr></tbody></table><h3>Planar relics</h3><p>Fear: Visage of Unbroken Will reveals the unseen with See Invisible, beside Spine of the Faceless and Dreadhusk of the Last Stand.</p><p>Hate: Maestro’s Unfinished Requiem grants Invisibility; Innoruuk’s Severed Covenant and Seal of the First Betrayal recall hatred and broken elven royalty.</p><p>Sky: Astrolabe of the Eighth Island grants ordinary Levitate, beside Veeshan’s Unwritten Horizon and Mantle of the First Brood.</p><p>Each click requires equipping the item at level 46 and a ten-second cast.</p></div></details><details class=\"change-entry\"><summary>Equipment &amp; trading: earlier update details</summary><div class=\"change-body\"><h2 id=\"equipment--loot-finder-preview\">Find ordinary equipment</h2><p>Use the loot finder to match your held classes and locate database-dropped equipment within the active era. <a href=\"loot-finder.html\">loot finder</a> <a href=\"items.html\">Hunt catalog</a> </p><p class=\"notice\">Full gear, AA and pet effects are not automatically modeled. <a href=\"build-lab.html\">Try the Build Lab</a> </p>\n<p class=\"notice\">The Classic raid rewards give every dungeon three exclusive designs. <a href=\"dungeon-modes.html#unique-rewards\">Classic raid rewards</a> </p>\n<h2 id=\"equipment--quest-ingredients\">Quest ingredient qualities -</h2><p>Normal-item quest requirements accept Polished, Exalted and Ascended versions of the same item.</p>\n<h2 id=\"equipment--classic-robes\">Classic race robes</h2><p>Game update 2026102204 repairs the model binding behind the waist gap reported on Barbarian and Half Elf.</p>\n<h2 id=\"equipment--thj-behavior-candidate\">THJ behavior and stock gear</h2><p>The custom AA, spell focus and stock-derived gear update is. <a href=\"unreleased.html#thj-behavior-candidate\">behavior details and open Play limits</a> </p><p>The update uses unmodified stock ProjectEQ as an approximation of standard EverQuest, then preserves the exact researched values where available.</p><table><thead><tr><th>Ascended field</th><th>Target from stock</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Positive AC, HP, mana, primary stats, resists, weapon damage and HP/mana regeneration</td><td>2×</td></tr><tr><td>Haste</td><td>1.5×, rounded</td></tr><tr><td>Spell Damage when stock has none</td><td>Higher of 2× INT or WIS</td></tr><tr><td>Healing Amount when stock has none</td><td>2× WIS</td></tr><tr><td>Accuracy when stock has none</td><td>Half DEX, rounded upward</td></tr><tr><td>New heroics</td><td>Quarter of the final matching stat, rounded; Ascended only</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Polished and Exalted receive one-third and two-thirds of the increase from Normal to Ascended.</p>\n<p class=\"notice\">Selected Ascended items now use THJ values, including reductions.</p>\n<p class=\"notice\">Browse the equipment catalog → Find a reward by slot, required level or source zone, with all four qualities grouped together. <a href=\"items.html\">Browse the equipment catalog →</a> </p></div></details><details class=\"change-entry\"><summary>Features: earlier update details</summary><div class=\"change-body\"><h2 id=\"features--hole-entrance\">The Hole entrance</h2><p class=\"notice\">— keyless Hole entrance: The Hole Key and lock-picking requirement have been removed from the entrance rock in Paineel at /loc 568,-896,-96.</p>\n<h2 id=\"features--loot-finder-preview\">Plan equipment for your classes</h2><p>The loot finder matches equipment usable by any held class, with an optional all-selected-classes mode, active-era filtering and source mobs, locations and calculated drop chances. <a href=\"loot-finder.html\">loot finder</a> </p><p class=\"notice\" id=\"features--hate-commonlands-candidate\">— Hate Keeper in Commonlands: Find the Plane of Hate Keeper in East Commonlands at /loc -1570,-346,3, between Mirielle and Khalure in the travel area.</p>\n<p class=\"notice\">Full gear, AA and pet effects are not automatically modeled. <a href=\"build-lab.html\">Try the Build Lab</a> </p>\n<p class=\"notice\">The Classic raid rewards give every dungeon three exclusive designs. <a href=\"dungeon-modes.html#unique-rewards\">Classic raid rewards</a> </p>\n<p class=\"notice\">Every Classic dungeon coverage adds the same Raid/Grind choices in 21 combat dungeon zones, including Fear, Hate and Sky. <a href=\"dungeon-modes.html#classic-candidate\">Every Classic dungeon coverage</a> </p>\n<h2 id=\"features--quest-ingredients-candidate\">Quest ingredient qualities -</h2><p>Better ordinary qualities can satisfy Normal quest ingredients, including the Aviak Charm for Crafted Gauntlets. <a href=\"equipment.html#quest-ingredients\">ingredient rules and limits</a> </p>\n<p class=\"notice\">Five class-armor families now give guaranteed Ascended rewards. <a href=\"unreleased.html#quest-quality\">guaranteed Ascended rewards</a> </p>\n<p class=\"notice\">Game update 2026102204 repairs the waist binding in the robe bodies added for seven Classic races. <a href=\"equipment.html#classic-robes\">Robe update</a> </p>\n<p class=\"notice\">Level-scaled AA: Earn two AA per level while leveling. <a href=\"multiclass.html#passive-abilities\">AA progression and examples</a> </p>\n<h2 id=\"features--thj-behavior-candidate\">THJ behavior and stock gear</h2><p>The custom AA, spell focus and stock-derived gear update is. <a href=\"unreleased.html#thj-behavior-candidate\">behavior details and open Play limits</a> </p>\n<p class=\"notice\">Live AA Play: All 16 classes have more earned AA options: 75 newly available lines, 111 expanded lines and Druid access to Healing Boon. <a href=\"multiclass.html#all-class-aa\">Read the AA update</a> </p>\n<p class=\"notice\">The combined item, spell, pet equipment and melee release is.</p>\n<p>Ordinary eligible equipment and bags have a 20% Polished, 5% Exalted and 1% Ascended chance per drop. <a href=\"equipment.html#item-tiers\">Read the loot quality rules</a> </p>\n<p class=\"feature-intro\">The major departures from Classic, with the rules you need before your next adventure.</p><p class=\"notice\"> <a href=\"unreleased.html\">More guides</a> </p><h2 id=\"features--character\">Build one character from three classes</h2><div class=\"feature-list\"><section class=\"feature-row\"><h3>Three classes from level 1</h3><div><p>Keep your starting class and choose two different extra classes.</p><a href=\"multiclass.html#three-classes\">Choose your classes →</a></div></section><section class=\"feature-row\"><h3>AA progression from the beginning</h3><div><p>Allowed AA ranks open at level 1.</p><a href=\"multiclass.html#passive-abilities\">Understand AA progression →</a></div></section><section class=\"feature-row\"><h3>Scribe spells ahead of time</h3><div><p>Eligible scrolls can enter your spellbook early.</p><a href=\"multiclass.html#spell-access\">Learn the spell rules →</a></div></section><section class=\"feature-row\"><h3>A roster of companions</h3><div><p>Multiple summoned pets, selected-pet or All-pets commands, and stored pet armor support a multiclass roster.</p><a href=\"pets.html\">Manage your pets →</a></div></section></div><h2 id=\"features--rewards\">Earn, trade and upgrade your gear</h2><div class=\"feature-list\"><section class=\"feature-row\"><h3>Stronger item qualities and zone rewards</h3><div><p>Ordinary tiered gear and the 48-zone reward hunt offer distinct quality families.</p><a href=\"zone-hunt.html\">Explore rewards and sockets →</a></div></section><section class=\"feature-row\"><h3>Turn duplicates into upgrades</h3><div><p>Use three Base zone rewards for Polished, then four matching copies for each higher step. <a href=\"item-upgrades.html#normal-items\">three identical eligible Normal/Base copies for Polished</a> </p><a href=\"item-upgrades.html\">See the upgrade recipes →</a></div></section><section class=\"feature-row\"><h3>Free trading and no LORE limit</h3><div><p>Trade formerly restricted and attuned items and keep duplicate LORE items.</p><a href=\"equipment.html#free-trade\">Read trading and resale rules →</a></div></section><section class=\"feature-row\"><h3>Equipment for your held classes</h3><div><p>Wear ordinary equipment allowed by any held class, regardless of playable race.</p><a href=\"multiclass.html#equipment-access\">Check equipment eligibility →</a></div></section></div><h2 id=\"features--adventuring\">Prepare in the tunnel, then explore</h2><div class=\"feature-list\"><section class=\"feature-row\"><h3>Raid or Grind in all 21 Classic dungeons</h3><div><p>Choose normal respawning enemies or harder enemies with permanent deaths.</p><a href=\"dungeon-modes.html\">Choose your dungeon mode →</a></div></section><section class=\"feature-row\"><h3>A shared home base</h3><div><p>New characters start with a kit and 100 platinum in the East Commonlands tunnel.</p><a href=\"tunnel.html\">Meet the tunnel services →</a></div></section><section class=\"feature-row\"><h3>Travel, discovery and private dungeons</h3><div><p>Use tunnel travel services, discover waypoint destinations and enter supported personal dungeon instances.</p><a href=\"travel.html\">Plan your journey →</a></div></section><section class=\"feature-row\"><h3>Lasting blessings; temporary combat abilities</h3><div><p>Ordinary beneficial blessings persist on players and owned pets.</p><a href=\"combat.html#buffs\">Know which effects last →</a></div></section><section class=\"feature-row\"><h3>Keep fighting while you cast</h3><div><p>Damage-over-time spells cast instantly, and melee autoattacks can continue during casting.</p><a href=\"combat.html#casting\">Read the combat changes →</a></div></section><section class=\"feature-row\"><h3>Less upkeep between adventures</h3><div><p>Food and drink are optional.</p><a href=\"combat.html\">Read combat and recovery →</a></div></section><section class=\"feature-row\"><h3>Healing without changing your target</h3><div><p>Ordinary heals can heal your own permanent pet.</p><a href=\"combat.html#healing\">Check healing targets →</a></div></section></div><h2 id=\"features--tools\">Spend more time playing</h2><div class=\"feature-list\"><section class=\"feature-row\"><h3>Stacked materials and Craft All</h3><div><p>Stackable items support at least 100, preserving larger limits.</p><a href=\"tradeskills.html\">Use the crafting controls →</a></div></section><section class=\"feature-row\"><h3>Advanced loot and bulk selling</h3><div><p>Use personal loot queues, loot preferences and group rolls.</p><a href=\"advanced-loot.html\">Learn the loot interface →</a></div></section><section class=\"feature-row\"><h3>One launcher, current updates</h3><div><p>The normal Nightcap shortcut delivers managed game/interface updates and dated patch summaries.</p><a href=\"launcher.html\">Update before playing →</a></div></section></div><h2 id=\"features--updates\">Keep up with changes</h2><p>Read Recent changes for dated updates. <a href=\"recent-changes.html\">Recent changes</a> </p><p class=\"notice\">Raid and Grind dungeon modes are available from all 21 dungeon Keepers. <a href=\"dungeon-modes.html\">Raid and Grind dungeon modes</a> </p>\n\n\n<h2 id=\"features--october-improvements\">More guidance and independent attacks</h2><p>The optional Recommended AA filter helps you choose early survival and damage upgrades. <a href=\"multiclass.html#recommended-aa\">Recommended AA filter</a> <a href=\"combat.html#monk-cooldowns\">Six basic Monk attacks have separate cooldowns</a> </p>\n<h2 id=\"features--thj-scaling\">Item and spell progression</h2><p>Ascended items, modest starter upgrades and stronger dungeon budgets bring item progression closer to the observed THJ references. <a href=\"equipment.html#reviewed-ascended\">Ascended items</a> <a href=\"combat.html#spell-scaling\">Additive Spell Damage and direct heroic-stat bonuses</a> </p>\n\n<h2 id=\"features--chapterhouse-candidate\">The Vigil of the Dawn</h2><p>Camil’s level-50 Paladin story in Chapterhouse uses Tasks, persistent personal chapters and a one-time helmet claim. <a href=\"camil-vigil.html\">Read the quest guide</a> <a href=\"zone-chapterhouse.html\">reward catalog</a> </p>\n</div></details><details class=\"change-entry\"><summary>Getting started: earlier update details</summary><div class=\"change-body\"><p class=\"notice\">Level-scaled AA: Earn two AA per level while leveling. <a href=\"multiclass.html#passive-abilities\">AA progression and examples</a> </p>\n<h2 id=\"getting-started--thj-behavior-candidate\">THJ behavior and stock gear</h2><p>The custom AA, spell focus and stock-derived gear update is. <a href=\"unreleased.html#thj-behavior-candidate\">behavior details and open Play limits</a> </p>\n<p class=\"notice\">Starter equipment now has modest quality upgrades.</p>\n<h2 id=\"getting-started--travel-files\">Repair missing Classic zone files</h2><p>Use the usual launcher Play flow for the Classic travel archive repair. <a href=\"launcher.html#zone-repair\">Classic travel archive repair</a> </p>\n<p>Nightcap is a solo-preferred progression server: thoughtful preparation, earned gear and encounter execution matter.</p>\n<p>Read Features first for the major ways Nightcap differs from Classic. <a href=\"features.html\">Read Features first</a> </p></div></details><details class=\"change-entry\"><summary>Welcome to the Nightcap Wiki: earlier update details</summary><div class=\"change-body\"><h2 id=\"index--hole-entrance\">The Hole entrance</h2><p class=\"notice\">— keyless Hole entrance: The Hole Key and lock-picking requirement have been removed from the entrance rock in Paineel at /loc 568,-896,-96.</p>\n<h2 id=\"index--loot-finder-preview\">Find your next upgrade</h2><p>Choose up to three held classes and find current-era equipment, its source mobs, locations and calculated drop chances. <a href=\"loot-finder.html\">Open the loot finder</a> </p><p class=\"notice\" id=\"index--hate-commonlands-candidate\">— Hate Keeper in Commonlands: Find the Plane of Hate Keeper in East Commonlands at /loc -1570,-346,3, between Mirielle and Khalure in the travel area.</p>\n<p class=\"notice\">The Classic raid rewards give every dungeon three exclusive designs. <a href=\"dungeon-modes.html#unique-rewards\">Classic raid rewards</a> </p>\n<p class=\"notice\">Every Classic dungeon coverage adds the same Raid/Grind choices in 21 combat dungeon zones, including Fear, Hate and Sky. <a href=\"dungeon-modes.html#classic-candidate\">Every Classic dungeon coverage</a> </p>\n<h2 id=\"index--quest-ingredients-candidate\">quest ingredient qualities</h2><p>Quest hand-ins and deliveries now accept Polished, Exalted and Ascended versions of Normal ingredients. <a href=\"equipment.html#quest-ingredients\">Try the Crafted Gauntlets turn-in and review the limits</a> </p>\n<p class=\"notice\">Crafted and four other class-armor families now award Ascended gear. <a href=\"unreleased.html#quest-quality\">Crafted and four other class-armor families</a> </p>\n<p class=\"notice\">The Classic robe waist correction is available for seven races. <a href=\"equipment.html#classic-robes\">Classic robe waist correction</a> </p>\n<p class=\"notice\">Level-scaled AA: Earn two AA per level while leveling. <a href=\"multiclass.html#passive-abilities\">AA progression and examples</a> </p>\n<h2 id=\"index--thj-behavior-candidate\">THJ behavior and stock gear</h2><p>The custom AA, spell focus and stock-derived gear update is. <a href=\"unreleased.html#thj-behavior-candidate\">behavior details and open Play limits</a> </p>\n<p class=\"notice\">Live AA Play: All 16 classes have more earned AA options: 75 newly available lines, 111 expanded lines and Druid access to Healing Boon. <a href=\"multiclass.html#all-class-aa\">Read the AA update</a> </p>\n<p class=\"notice\">Launch repair published: Game update 2026101901 corrects the client catalog mismatch that blocked Play after the previous update.</p>\n<p class=\"notice\">The item/spell and pet/melee release is available.</p>\n<p>Ordinary loot quality chances are now 20% Polished, 5% Exalted and 1% Ascended per eligible item drop. <a href=\"equipment.html#item-tiers\">Loot quality details</a> </p><p class=\"notice\">October 18 update:Independent AA cooldowns and item/discipline timer repairs are available. <a href=\"combat.html#ability-cooldowns\">Independent AA cooldowns and item/discipline timer repairs</a> </p><p>October 18:Classic travel archive repair is available through normal launcher Play, including West Commonlands. <a href=\"launcher.html#zone-repair\">Classic travel archive repair</a> </p>\n<p class=\"notice\">October 17 update:Recommended AA, passive AA while leveling, no normal-death EXP loss, stacks of at least 100, three-Normal reforging and independent Monk attacks are available. <a href=\"multiclass.html#recommended-aa\">Recommended AA</a> <a href=\"combat.html#death-exp\">no normal-death EXP loss</a> </p>\n<div class=\"welcome\"><div class=\"welcome-copy\"><p class=\"eyebrow\">A familiar world.</p><h2>Three classes.<br>One more adventure.</h2><p>Find your build, learn the custom systems, and discover what is waiting beyond the tunnel.</p><a class=\"button\" href=\"getting-started.html\">Start your journey →</a></div><img src=\"assets/traders-at-dusk.png\" width=\"1672\" height=\"941\" alt=\"Nightcap traders beneath lanterns in a stone tunnel at dusk.\"></div><div class=\"facts\"><span><strong>Classic</strong> current era</span><span><strong>50</strong> level cap</span><span><strong>3</strong> classes per character</span><span><strong>48</strong> reward zones</span></div><p class=\"feature-entry\">New to Nightcap?Explore Features — the major changes from Classic → <a href=\"features.html\">Explore Features — the major changes from Classic →</a> </p><div class=\"portal-grid\"><section class=\"portal\"><h2>Character &amp; classes</h2><ul><li><a href=\"multiclass.html\">Multiclass &amp; progression</a><small>Choose your classes, skills and abilities.</small></li><li><a href=\"pets.html\">Pets &amp; pet armor</a><small>Your companions, commands and loadouts.</small></li></ul></section><section class=\"portal\"><h2>Items &amp; equipment</h2><ul><li><a href=\"items.html\">Browse equipment</a><small>Find gear and augments by slot, level and zone.</small></li><li><a href=\"zone-hunt.html\">Zone hunt &amp; forging</a><small>Drop chances, heroic augments and upgrades.</small></li><li><a href=\"equipment.html\">Equipment &amp; trading</a><small>Existing tiers, bags and selling rules.</small></li></ul></section><section class=\"portal\"><h2>Explore the world</h2><ul><li><a href=\"zones.html\">Zones &amp; rewards</a><small>48 Classic destinations and their rewards.</small></li><li><a href=\"tunnel.html\">East Commonlands tunnel</a><small>Trainers, merchants and blessings.</small></li><li><a href=\"travel.html\">Travel &amp; instances</a><small>Find your way out. Find your way home.</small></li></ul></section><section class=\"portal\"><h2>Adventures &amp; quests</h2><ul><li><a href=\"advanced-loot.html\">Advanced loot</a><small>Personal drops, filters and group rolls.</small></li><li><a href=\"ascension.html\">Ascension quest</a><small>Reforge your original class epic.</small></li><li><a href=\"waypoints.html\">Waypoint Explorer</a><small>Discover destinations and earn a title.</small></li></ul></section></div><div class=\"home-columns\"><section><h2>New in Nightcap</h2><p>Raid or Grind in all 21 Classic dungeons. <a href=\"dungeon-modes.html\">Raid or Grind in all 21 Classic dungeons.</a> </p><p>Build, craft and upgrade. <a href=\"item-upgrades.html#normal-items\">normal-item box recipe</a> </p><p>Passive AA is now 10% alongside normal leveling. <a href=\"recent-changes.html\">Guide</a> </p></section><section><h2>At the campfire</h2><ul><li><a href=\"commands.html\">Keep the command reference handy</a></li><li><a href=\"launcher.html\">Update your launcher and game</a></li><li><a href=\"combat.html\">Read about combat and recovery</a></li><li><a href=\"unreleased.html\">See what is still in development</a></li></ul><p class=\"notice\">Nightcap is available.</p></section></div>\n\n\n\n<h2 id=\"index--chapterhouse-candidate\">The Vigil of the Dawn</h2><p>Camil’s Vigil of the Dawn is available. <a href=\"camil-vigil.html\">Read the quest guide</a> <a href=\"zone-chapterhouse.html\">reward catalog</a> </p>\n</div></details><details class=\"change-entry\"><summary>Item upgrades: earlier update details</summary><div class=\"change-body\"><h2 id=\"item-upgrades--quest-ingredients-candidate\">Quest ingredient qualities -</h2><p>Ordinary quality variants can satisfy Normal quest requirements. <a href=\"equipment.html#quest-ingredients\">Ordinary quality variants can satisfy Normal quest requirements</a> </p>\n<h2 id=\"item-upgrades--thj-behavior-candidate\">THJ behavior and stock gear</h2><p>The custom AA, spell focus and stock-derived gear update is. <a href=\"unreleased.html#thj-behavior-candidate\">behavior details and open Play limits</a> </p><p>The update changes stats on existing ordinary qualities.</p>\n<p class=\"notice\">Selected Ascended values and intermediate stats have been retuned while retaining item identities, effects and sockets.</p>\n<p>Nightcap has two forgeable tier families: ordinary tiered equipment ends at Ascended, while the Classic zone-hunt rewards end at Ascension.</p>\n</div></details><details class=\"change-entry\"><summary>Launcher &amp; interface: earlier update details</summary><div class=\"change-body\"><h2 id=\"launcher--classic-robes-candidate\">Classic robe waist correction</h2><p>Game update 2026102204 repairs model binding on the added Classic robe bodies after the earlier 2026102203 repair failed. <a href=\"equipment.html#classic-robes\">Affected races and Play status</a> </p>\n<p class=\"notice\">Launch repair published: Game update 2026101901 corrects the client catalog mismatch that blocked Play after the previous update.</p>\n<p class=\"notice\">Game update 2026101802 pairs the expanded pet Equipment tab and spell/AA descriptions with the new server release.</p>\n<h2 id=\"launcher--zone-repair\">Classic travel file checks</h2><p>Game update 2026101801 adds terrain and object archive checks for 17 Classic travel destinations, including West Commonlands, Misty Thicket and Toxxulia.</p>\n<h2 id=\"launcher--startup-repairs\">Startup and character-selection repairs</h2><p>Updates repair model archives and missing materials behind the recent Play and character-selection failures.</p>\n<h2 id=\"launcher--animation-repairs\">Creature and pet animation repairs</h2><p>The latest updates repair shared creature animations and Enchanter weapon-pet identity.</p>\n\n<h2 id=\"launcher--october-release\">October 17 gameplay update</h2><p>Close EverQuest and choose Play to receive the Recommended AA window and independent Monk attack timers.</p></div></details><details class=\"change-entry\"><summary>Multiclass &amp; progression: earlier update details</summary><div class=\"change-body\"><h2 id=\"multiclass--loot-finder-preview\">Search gear for your held classes</h2><p>The loot finder defaults to Any held class, matching Nightcap equipment access. <a href=\"loot-finder.html\">loot finder</a> </p><p class=\"notice\">Robe appearance: Game update 2026102204 repairs the robe waist binding for seven Classic races. <a href=\"equipment.html#classic-robes\">Affected races and Play status</a> </p>\n<p class=\"notice\">Level-scaled AA: Earn two AA per level while leveling. <a href=\"multiclass.html#passive-abilities\">AA progression and examples</a> </p>\n<h2 id=\"multiclass--thj-behavior-candidate\">THJ behavior and stock gear</h2><p>The custom AA, spell focus and stock-derived gear update is. <a href=\"unreleased.html#thj-behavior-candidate\">behavior details and open Play limits</a> </p><p>AA changes include group Act of Valor, 40% Harvest and percentage-based Mana Burn. Silent Casting, Warrior debuffs and Wizard abilities also change. </p>\n<p class=\"notice\">Live AA Play: All 16 classes have more earned AA options: 75 newly available lines, 111 expanded lines and Druid access to Healing Boon. <a href=\"multiclass.html#all-class-aa\">Read the AA update</a> </p>\n<p class=\"notice\">earned pet and melee AA ranks and held-class combat benefits are available.</p>\n</div></details><details class=\"change-entry\"><summary>Pets &amp; pet armor: earlier update details</summary><div class=\"change-body\"><h2 id=\"pets--thj-behavior-candidate\">THJ behavior and stock gear</h2><p>The custom AA, spell focus and stock-derived gear update is. <a href=\"unreleased.html#thj-behavior-candidate\">behavior details and open Play limits</a> </p><p>The focus changes apply to players and permanent pets.</p>\n<p class=\"notice\">Permanent-pet equipment has three pages with 22 locations. Mage pets can hold 15 items. Other permanent class pets can hold eight. </p>\n</div></details><details class=\"change-entry\"><summary>Travel &amp; instances: earlier update details</summary><div class=\"change-body\"><h2 id=\"travel--hole-entrance\">The Hole entrance</h2><p class=\"notice\">— keyless Hole entrance: The Hole Key and lock-picking requirement have been removed from the entrance rock in Paineel at /loc 568,-896,-96.</p>\n<p class=\"notice\" id=\"travel--hate-commonlands-candidate\">— Hate Keeper in Commonlands: Find the Plane of Hate Keeper in East Commonlands at /loc -1570,-346,3, between Mirielle and Khalure in the travel area.</p>\n<p class=\"notice\">The Classic raid rewards give every dungeon three exclusive designs. <a href=\"dungeon-modes.html#unique-rewards\">Classic raid rewards</a> </p>\n<p class=\"notice\">Every Classic dungeon coverage adds the same Raid/Grind choices in 21 combat dungeon zones, including Fear, Hate and Sky. <a href=\"dungeon-modes.html#classic-candidate\">Every Classic dungeon coverage</a> </p>\n<p class=\"notice\">The separate level-65/Planes of Power profile and its additional merchant stock remain staged.</p>\n<h2 id=\"travel--missing-zone-files\">If a Classic destination fails to load</h2><p>Close EverQuest and use launcher Play to install game update 2026101801 or newer.</p>\n</div></details><details class=\"change-entry\"><summary>East Commonlands tunnel: earlier update details</summary><div class=\"change-body\"><h2 id=\"tunnel--experience-blessing\">XP blessing retired</h2><p>Magus Goldwind no longer charges platinum or grants the XP package.</p>\n</div></details><details class=\"change-entry\"><summary>More guides: earlier update details</summary><div class=\"change-body\"><p class=\"notice\" id=\"unreleased--hate-commonlands-candidate\">— Hate Keeper in Commonlands: Find the Plane of Hate Keeper in East Commonlands at /loc -1570,-346,3, between Mirielle and Khalure in the travel area.</p>\n<p class=\"notice\">The Classic raid rewards give every dungeon three exclusive designs. <a href=\"dungeon-modes.html#unique-rewards\">Classic raid rewards</a> </p>\n<p class=\"notice\">Every Classic dungeon coverage adds the same Raid/Grind choices in 21 combat dungeon zones, including Fear, Hate and Sky. <a href=\"dungeon-modes.html#classic-candidate\">Every Classic dungeon coverage</a> </p>\n<h2 id=\"unreleased--quest-ingredients\">Quest ingredient qualities -</h2><p>The fix for rejection of Aviak Charm (Polished) is deployed. <a href=\"equipment.html#quest-ingredients\">explicit-quality and forging rules remain separate</a> </p>\n<h2 id=\"unreleased--crystal-markers\">Waypoint crystals</h2><p>Waypoints now have a glowing crystal with the existing a waypoint label.</p>\n<h2 id=\"unreleased--classic-robes\">Classic robe waist correction</h2><p>Game update 2026102204 repairs the waist binding after the earlier 2026102203 repair failed on Barbarian and Half Elf. <a href=\"equipment.html#classic-robes\">Update details</a> </p>\n<h2 id=\"unreleased--befallen-keeper\">Dungeon Keeper visibility</h2><p>The placement correction now covers all five confirmed waypoint overlaps: Befallen, Unrest, Najena, Permafrost and Nagafen’s Lair. <a href=\"dungeon-modes.html\">Keeper locations</a> </p>\n<h2 id=\"unreleased--thj-behavior-candidate\">THJ behavior and stock gear</h2><p>The custom AA, spell focus and stock-derived gear update is. <a href=\"unreleased.html#thj-behavior-candidate\">behavior details and open Play limits</a> </p><h3>Custom AA behavior</h3><ul><li>Warlord’s Fury: +100% physical skill damage for up to 12 seconds, 60-second reuse.</li><li>Gut Punch: initial damage and +50% physical damage taken for up to 12 seconds. Press the Attack lowers AC; Grappling Strike lowers evasion. </li><li>Act of Valor: spends 50% of maximum mana once and heals nearby group members for 2 HP per mana spent.</li><li>Harvest: activate to restore 40% maximum mana.</li><li>Mana Burn/Blast/Blaze/Volatile Mana Blaze: spend 10/20/30/40% maximum mana; keep 4 damage per mana as a tuning choice. All reach 15-minute reuse with full Hastened Manaburn. Target immunity rejects the cast without mana or cooldown loss.</li><li>Silent Casting: all casting classes, one-hour duration, 60-second reuse, suspendable timer. Subtlety and obsolete haste/duration modifiers refund purchased ranks.</li><li>Dimensional Shielding: separate Wizard AA protecting casting from hits, movement and hostile interrupt effects. Stuns and voluntary cancellation still interrupt. Its 120-second duration and 30-minute reuse are kept-value tuning choices.</li><li>Pyromancy/Cryomancy: 35% proc chance, initial damage plus DoT, opposite-element resistance reduction and compatibility with other buffs. Existing level/mana/trigger restrictions remain.</li></ul><h3>Evidence and Play limits</h3><p>The stock baseline is ProjectEQ, not a recovered THJ or Daybreak database.</p>\n<h2 id=\"unreleased--all-class-aa\">All-class AAs are now in</h2><p>The rank and access update is installed. <a href=\"multiclass.html#all-class-aa\">the released AA rules</a> </p>\n<h2 id=\"unreleased--thj-parity\">Item and spell scaling is now in</h2><p>The combined release is installed. <a href=\"equipment.html\">Equipment</a> <a href=\"combat.html\">Combat</a> </p><h2 id=\"unreleased--wpm-melee\">Shield and melee changes are now in</h2><p>The earned held-class melee and shield changes shipped with the combined release. <a href=\"combat.html#melee-builds\">the combat guide</a> </p><h2 id=\"unreleased--pet-scaling\">Separate level-65 and Planes of Power profile</h2><p>The expanded pet equipment and scaling changes are installed, but the level-65/Planes of Power profile and 389 additional merchant entries are still staged.</p>\n<h2 id=\"unreleased--quest-quality\">Guaranteed quality for substantial class armor</h2><p>The installed update grants existing Ascended versions of 37 Crafted, Lambent, Darkforge, Ivy Etched and Totemic quest rewards.</p><p>The 37 rewards are live.</p><h2 id=\"unreleased--cooldown-identities\">Remaining shared skill and spell cooldowns</h2><p>The AA and cross-ability timer correction is deployed. <a href=\"combat.html#ability-cooldowns\">AA and cross-ability timer correction is deployed</a> </p>\n<h2 id=\"unreleased--journal\">Adventure Journal prototype — historical status</h2><p>The original eight quests and charm were built as an uninstalled prototype. <a href=\"#last-lantern-20261107\">November7 Last Lantern release</a> </p>\n<h2 id=\"unreleased--combat\">Combat and item candidates</h2><p>The separate extra-class skill, trainer and offhand correction is deployed; the reported player issue was confirmed resolved. <a href=\"multiclass.html#earned-skills\">extra-class skill, trainer and offhand correction</a> </p>\n<h2 id=\"unreleased--testing\">System guides</h2><p>See Features for the available systems. <a href=\"features.html\">Features</a> </p>\n\n<h2 id=\"unreleased--chapterhouse-candidate\">The Vigil of the Dawn</h2><p>The Vigil of the Dawn has moved into. <a href=\"camil-vigil.html\">Read the quest guide</a> <a href=\"zone-chapterhouse.html\">reward catalog</a> </p>\n</div></details><details class=\"change-entry\"><summary>Waypoint Explorer: earlier update details</summary><div class=\"change-body\"><h2 id=\"waypoints--crystal-markers\">Waypoint crystals</h2><p>Waypoints now have a glowing crystal with the existing a waypoint label.</p>\n</div></details>\n\n<h2 id=\"paladin-weapon-grip-20261026\">October 26, 2026 — Paladin weapon grips</h2><p>a right-click 1HS/2HS toggle is available for SoulFire, Fiery Avenger and Fiery Defender, including existing quality variants. <a href=\"equipment.html#paladin-weapon-grip\">Grip instructions</a> </p>\n<h2 id=\"paladin-grip-repair-20261027\">October27 grip issue and October28 paired repair</h2><p>SoulFire could report 1HS while the client kept a two-handed definition. <a href=\"equipment.html#paladin-weapon-grip\">Stats and grip instructions</a> </p><h2 id=\"bazaar-ui-repair-20261028\">October28 — missing Bazaar controls</h2><p>The update also corrects a Bazaar XML parsing error that made the entire Nightcap interface fall back to Default.</p>\n<h2 id=\"bazaar-startup-crash-20261028\">October 28: Bazaar startup crash — client hotfix 2026102802</h2><p>Client hotfix 2026102802 corrects missing Bazaar tab borders that caused a crash during world entry.</p>\n<h2 id=\"hate-layout-20261029\">October 29: Plane of Hate ground-level layout</h2><p>New Raid and Grind runs use the newer Hate layout. Existing encounters, enemy strength, loot, experience and completion rewards remain. <a href=\"dungeon-modes.html#hate-layout-preview\">Entry and landmarks</a> </p>\n\n<h2 id=\"keyless-doors-20261029\">October 29: keyless doors</h2><p>Keys and lock picks are no longer required for ordinary locked doors throughout existing door content. <a href=\"travel.html#keyless-doors\">Door access and remaining restrictions</a> </p>\n\n\n<h2 id=\"cast-bar-repair-20261030\">October 30: spell casting bar timing — reported issue resolved</h2><p>Client update 2026103002 corrects casting bars that stayed full until the final instant. <a href=\"launcher.html#cast-bar-repair\">Update instructions</a> </p>\n<h2 id=\"hate-boss-placement-20261030\">October 30: Hate boss landmark correction</h2><p>Corrected the ground-level substitute locations for Maestro, the Hand and Innoruuk to their organ/platform/throne landmarks.</p>\n\n<h2 id=\"augment-description-correction\">November6: augment descriptions and equipped totals</h2><p>Client0.13.3 shows Hunt Shield Block in the item Description with its shield and strongest-only restrictions. <a href=\"augment-audit.html#augment-description-correction\">Instructions and stacking</a> </p>\n<h2 id=\"augment-icon-candidate\">November 12: augment icon correction</h2><p>Ordinary stat augments now preserve equipment icons and existing cosmetic transformations. <a href=\"equipment.html#augment-icon-candidate\">Equipment guidance</a> </p><h2 id=\"earned-titles-20261112\">November 12: earned titles</h2><p>A Titles reference describes 77 cosmetic unlocks and their exact requirements. <a href=\"titles.html\">Titles reference</a> </p>",
+  "body": "<h2 id=\"inventory-no-scrollbars\">November 20: Inventory scrollbars removed</h2><p>The main Inventory tab no longer has horizontal or vertical scrollbars. The separate Stats tab still scrolls. Fully exit EverQuest and press Play in the launcher. <a href=\"equipment.html#inventory-combat-summary\">Inventory guide</a>.</p><h2 id=\"titles-automatic-suffix\">November 14: automatic titles and matching suffixes</h2><p>Titles now unlock automatically when earned, with a chat message and a new-title alert. Every prefix also unlocks a matching suffix through the same achievement. Existing awards gain their matching suffix without another grind. Login and zoning automatically check recorded goals. <code>#titles</code> remains an optional progress list. <a href=\"titles.html\">Title names and requirements</a>.</p><h2 id=\"titles-active\">November 14: earned titles available</h2><p>The <a href=\"titles.html\">77 cosmetic titles</a> and <code>#titles</code> are available. Open the Titles window to check existing completion and skill goals. New slayer totals start now. Nagafen earns Flamebreaker; defeating both Nagafen and Vox earns Dragonslayer. Newly earned titles notify you and never replace your selected title.</p><h2 id=\"backstab-weapons\">November 13 · Backstab weapons</h2><p>Backstab now uses the stronger qualifying weapon in either hand. See <a href=\"combat.html#backstab-weapons\">how Backstab chooses your weapon</a>.</p><h2 id=\"bow-damage\">November 13 · Bow damage</h2><p>Heroic Dexterity now increases damage from ordinary bow shots. See the <a href=\"combat.html#bow-damage\">bow damage table and Archery Mastery ranks</a>.</p><h2 id=\"stock-sympathetic\">November 13 · Classic sympathetic clicks</h2><p>The Ascended Runed Lava Pendant now grants Sympathetic Strike I. The Ascended Moonstone Ring grants Sympathetic Healing I. Exit EverQuest. Select Play in the Nightcap launcher to get the new spell descriptions. See <a href=\"equipment.html#stock-sympathetic\">item sources, eligible spells and bonus amounts</a>.</p><h2 id=\"wiki-simple-20261113\">November 13: wiki layout</h2><p>The wiki has a simpler layout, shorter guides and direct topic links.</p><h2 id=\"stock-worn-atk\">November 13 · Stock equipment ATK</h2><p>Polished, Exalted and Ascended versions of 135 stock families now use updated worn ATK. <a href=\"equipment.html#stock-worn-atk\">See all item values and how the cap works</a> </p><h2 id=\"classic-raid-augments\">November 12 · Classic raid boss augments</h2><p>Classic raid augments drop from 25 named bosses. <a href=\"classic-raid-augments.html\">Classic raid augments</a> </p><h2 id=\"inventory-combat-summary\">November 12: Inventory combat stats, caps and heroics</h2><p>Signed client 2026111202 with proxy 0.13.6 adds the combat summary and current/cap/heroic attributes to the main Inventory tab. <a href=\"equipment.html#inventory-combat-summary\">Instructions</a> </p>\n<h2 id=\"dot-initial-damage-20261112\">November 12: DoT initial damage removed</h2><p>Player DoTs no longer deal their separate cast-time damage hit. <a href=\"combat.html#dot-initial-damage\">Timing details</a> </p>\n<h2 id=\"imitate-death\">November 12: Imitate Death without cooldown</h2><p>Removed Imitate Death's ability cooldown and retired its old saved wait. <a href=\"combat.html#imitate-death\">Hotkey instructions and limits</a> </p>\n<h2 id=\"quick-buff-hotkey-fix-20261112\">November 12: Quick Buff hotkey creation fixed</h2><p>Fixed the disabled Make Hotkey button for players who own Quick Buff. <a href=\"combat.html#quick-buff-hotkey-ready\">Hotkey instructions</a> </p>\n<h2 id=\"quick-buff-20261112\">November 12: Quick Buff hotkey</h2><p>Quick Buff replaces passive buff haste with an activated hotkey that immediately casts eligible memorized buffs for 50% maximum mana with no reuse delay. <a href=\"combat.html#quick-buff-hotkey\">Hotkey instructions</a> </p>\n<h2 id=\"last-lantern-20261107\">November7: The Last Lantern</h2><p>The Adventure Journal continues to level 50. Complete eight private memories, choose from five oath paths and earn an eight-piece armor outfit. <a href=\"adventure-journal.html\">Start, chapters and rewards</a> </p>\n<h2 id=\"advanced-loot-repair-20261107\">November 7: Advanced Loot client repair</h2><p>Client 2026110605 repairs automatic opening after closing Filters and visibility after a skin reload, including new loot beyond the first page. <a href=\"advanced-loot.html#row-controls\">Controls and update instructions</a> </p>\n<span id=\"keeper-readiness-20261106\"></span><p>Raid and Grind entry now accepts the current expedition augment release.</p><h2 id=\"shield-block-total\">November6: one Shield Block total</h2><p>Update2026110604 keeps a single Shield Block row, including equipped augment bonuses, and removes the redundant augment-only breakdown.</p>\n<h2 id=\"stats-font\">November6: Stats font and Hunt label</h2><p>Update2026110603 matches the added Stats rows to the normal font and row height.</p>\n<h2 id=\"character-stats-window\">November6: automatic equipped Stats</h2><p>Signed client0.13.4/update2026110602 adds Shield Block, Hunt contribution, relative Dodge, item focus potential and worn Faerune to Inventory Stats. <a href=\"equipment.html#augment-description-correction\">How to check your stats</a> </p>\n<h2 id=\"augment-audit-20261106\">November6: zone augments and exotic icons</h2><p>Augments can drop from any unowned killable NPC in enabled zones, including guards, named enemies, killable merchants and scripted adds. <a href=\"augment-audit.html\">Full list and limits</a> </p><h2 id=\"hunt-rates-20261101\">November 1: zone augments drop three times as often - live</h2><p>Zone Hunt augments now drop at 1.5% per eligible kill (was 0.5%), about one per 67 kills. <a href=\"zone-hunt.html#drops\">How drops work</a> </p><h2 id=\"ssf-20261101\">November 1: solo self-found mode -</h2><p>New level-1 characters can swear a permanent solo self-found oath at the Ancient Chronicler. <a href=\"multiclass.html#solo-self-found\">How it works</a> </p><h2 id=\"hate-density-20261030\">October 30: Plane of Hate density -</h2><p> <a href=\"dungeon-modes.html#hate-layout-preview\">Hate modes and landmarks</a> </p>\n<h2 id=\"public-cazic-20261030\">October 30 — public Classic Cazic-Thule restored</h2><p>Restored 188 Classic encounter points in open-world Cazic-Thule, which previously had no eligible combat population under Classic.</p><h2 id=\"recall-labels-20261030\">October 30: Commonlands recall labels corrected</h2><p class=\"notice\">Recall labels corrected (October 30): Client release 2026103001 restores Ancient Attunement’s name, Nightcap Recall’s hotbutton label and the recall description.</p>\n<details class=\"change-entry\" open><summary>October28: Bazaar posting and readable controls</summary><div class=\"change-body\"><p>Client update2026102803 accepts valid whole-platinum digits in both text formats, reports unreadable input, and enlarges seller text with light colors.</p></div></details><details class=\"change-entry\" open><summary>October 26: Bazaar seller panel and Paladin grips</summary><div class=\"change-body\"><h2 id=\"bazaar-panel-candidate\">Sell / My Listings controls</h2><p>Client update 2026102601 adds the Sell / My Listings tab for posting, cancelling owned listings and collecting offline proceeds. <a href=\"tunnel.html#bazaar-seller-panel\">Panel instructions</a> </p></div></details><h2 id=\"commonlands-bazaar-20261026\">October 26: Commonlands player bazaar</h2><p>Persistent player listings, offline seller proceeds and search/purchase routing are installed in public East Commonlands. <a href=\"tunnel.html#player-bazaar\">Market instructions and restrictions</a> </p>\n<h2 id=\"october24-coordinated\">October 24 — High Keep rescue, Ashen Compact and aggro corrections</h2><p>New High Keep Raid runs now rescue Osargen.</p>\n<h2 id=\"ashen-compact-everfrost\">October 24 — Ashen Compact entrance</h2><p>Its frostbound crossing and return connect to custom Kael. <a href=\"ashen-compact.html\">Shadow Knight campaign</a> </p><h2 id=\"rogue-tome-learning\">October 24 - Multiclass tome learning repaired</h2><p>Eligible tomes can now be learned through any held class, fixing secondary and third-class Rogue learning. <a href=\"multiclass.html#learning-tomes\">learning combat disciplines</a> </p><h2 id=\"custom-feature-directory\">October 24 — Custom content on Features</h2><p>Features now groups Raid &amp; Grind dungeons, helmet quests, Zone Hunt, epic reforging, class armor, crafting, exploration and custom character systems. <a href=\"features.html\">Features</a> </p><p>Current instructions live in Guides. <a href=\"all-pages.html\">Guides</a> </p><details class=\"change-entry\" id=\"wiki-clarity\" open><summary>October 24, 2026 · A clearer wiki</summary><div class=\"change-body\"><p>Features now highlights the major differences from standard EQ.</p></div></details><details class=\"change-entry\" id=\"hole-entrance\"><summary>October 24 · The Hole entrance</summary><div class=\"change-body\"><p class=\"notice\">— keyless Hole entrance: The Hole Key and lock-picking requirement have been removed from the entrance rock in Paineel at /loc 568,-896,-96.</p>\n</div></details><details class=\"change-entry\" id=\"aa-level-progression\"><summary>October 23: two AA per level and level-1 AA controls</summary><div class=\"change-body\"><p>The paired update is.</p>\n</div></details><details class=\"change-entry\" id=\"chapterhouse-candidate\"><summary>October 23 · The Vigil of the Dawn</summary><div class=\"change-body\"><p>October 23: Camil’s Chapterhouse quest, level-50–53 encounters, custom rewards, Ember augment, waypoint and Keeper are deployed. <a href=\"camil-vigil.html\">Read the quest guide</a> <a href=\"zone-chapterhouse.html\">reward catalog</a> </p>\n</div></details><details class=\"change-entry\" id=\"loot-finder-preview\"><summary>October 22: production loot finder</summary><div class=\"change-body\"><p>The Loot finder supports class, slot, quality, level and zone filters. Item links show enemy sources, locations and drop chances. <a href=\"loot-finder.html\">class and era loot finder</a> </p><p class=\"notice\" id=\"hate-commonlands-candidate\">— Hate Keeper in Commonlands: Find the Plane of Hate Keeper in East Commonlands at /loc -1570,-346,3, between Mirielle and Khalure in the travel area.</p>\n</div></details><details class=\"change-entry\" id=\"build-lab\"><summary>Build Lab — October 22</summary><div class=\"change-body\"><p>The Build Lab compares two saved builds, supported spell benefits, Hunt item stat differences and editable ability priorities. <a href=\"build-lab.html\">Build Lab</a> </p>\n</div></details><details class=\"change-entry\" id=\"interactive-handbook\"><summary>October 22 — Your interactive field guide</summary><div class=\"change-body\"><p>The wiki has a new lantern-lit design with four adventure paths, instant quick search, saved guides, light and dark reading modes, and a reading-progress bar. <a href=\"about.html#navigation\">Learn the shortcuts and field notes →</a> </p><p class=\"notice\">The Classic raid rewards give every dungeon three exclusive designs. <a href=\"dungeon-modes.html#unique-rewards\">Classic raid rewards</a> </p>\n</div></details><details class=\"change-entry\" id=\"classic-dungeons-candidate\"><summary>October 22 — every Classic dungeon and unique rewards live</summary><div class=\"change-body\"><p class=\"notice\">Every Classic dungeon coverage adds the same Raid/Grind choices in 21 combat dungeon zones, including Fear, Hate and Sky. <a href=\"dungeon-modes.html#classic-candidate\">Every Classic dungeon coverage</a> </p>\n<p>The paired release also repairs stale dungeon item checks behind the reported Keeper error and installs durable Sky key services.</p>\n</div></details><details class=\"change-entry\" id=\"quest-ingredients-20261022\"><summary>October 22 - quest ingredient fix live for Play</summary><div class=\"change-body\"><p>Polished, Exalted and Ascended ingredients can satisfy Normal quest requirements, including Aviak Charm for Crafted Gauntlets. <a href=\"equipment.html#quest-ingredients\">Scope and limits</a> </p>\n</div></details><details class=\"change-entry\" id=\"class-armor-candidate\"><summary>October 22 — Ascended class-armor quest rewards</summary><div class=\"change-body\"><p>Crafted, Lambent, Darkforge, Ivy Etched and Totemic quests now grant 37 Ascended armor rewards. <a href=\"unreleased.html#quest-quality\">Reward guide</a> </p>\n</div></details><details class=\"change-entry\" id=\"crystal-markers\"><summary>October 22 · Waypoint crystals</summary><div class=\"change-body\"><p>Waypoints now have a glowing crystal with the existing a waypoint label.</p>\n</div></details><details class=\"change-entry\" id=\"classic-robes-20261022\"><summary>October 22 — robe waist correction in</summary><div class=\"change-body\"><p>Game update 2026102204 repairs the waist binding after the earlier 2026102203 repair failed, covering all seven added Classic robe races and both genders. <a href=\"equipment.html#classic-robes\">Read the scope</a> </p>\n</div></details><details class=\"change-entry\" id=\"keeper-visibility-20261022\"><summary>October 22 — Dungeon Keeper placement</summary><div class=\"change-body\"><p>The correction now separates Keepers from overlapping waypoints in Befallen, Unrest, Najena, Permafrost and Nagafen’s Lair. <a href=\"dungeon-modes.html\">All seven Keeper locations</a> </p>\n<p class=\"notice\">Level-scaled AA: Earn two AA per level while leveling. <a href=\"multiclass.html#passive-abilities\">AA progression and examples</a> </p></div></details><details class=\"change-entry\" id=\"aa-million-xp\"><summary>October 21: slower AA earning and XP boost retirement</summary><div class=\"change-body\"><p>The October 21 release used 1,000,000 AA experience per point with 10% passive earning; the October 23 level-scaled update supersedes that earning model.</p>\n</div></details><details class=\"change-entry\" id=\"thj-behavior-candidate\"><summary>October 19 · THJ behavior and stock gear</summary><div class=\"change-body\"><p>The custom AA, spell focus and stock-derived gear update is. <a href=\"unreleased.html#thj-behavior-candidate\">behavior details and open Play limits</a> </p>\n</div></details><details class=\"change-entry\" id=\"all-class-aa-20261019\"><summary>October 19: all-class AA update</summary><div class=\"change-body\"><p class=\"notice\">Live AA Play: All 16 classes have more earned AA options: 75 newly available lines, 111 expanded lines and Druid access to Healing Boon. <a href=\"multiclass.html#all-class-aa\">Read the AA update</a> </p>\n<p class=\"notice\">Launch repair published: Game update 2026101901 corrects the client catalog mismatch that blocked Play after the previous update.</p>\n</div></details><details class=\"change-entry\" id=\"thj-release\"><summary>October 18: item, spell, pet and melee release</summary><div class=\"change-body\"><p>Selected Ascended items now use THJ values.</p><p>Permanent-pet equipment now has pages. The update also changes pet and melee AAs, Rabid Bear effects and shared stat limits. </p>\n<h2>October 18 - More ordinary quality loot</h2><p>Polished, Exalted and Ascended now have 20%, 5% and 1% chances per eligible ordinary equipment/bag drop.</p></div></details><details class=\"change-entry\" id=\"reforge-colors\"><summary>October 18, 2026: built-in item colors</summary><div class=\"change-body\"><p>The Reforging Box and zone forging now accept an item's built-in color. <a href=\"item-upgrades.html#requirements\">Reforging Box</a> <a href=\"zone-hunt.html#forging\">zone forging</a> </p>\n</div></details><details class=\"change-entry\" id=\"october-18-cooldowns\"><summary>October 18, 2026: separate ability cooldowns</summary><div class=\"change-body\"><p>Activated AA families now have independent cooldowns, including Rampage and Purify Body. <a href=\"combat.html#ability-cooldowns\">Activated AA families now have independent cooldowns</a> <a href=\"unreleased.html#cooldown-identities\">generic skill and content-defined groups</a> </p>\n</div></details><details class=\"change-entry\" id=\"october-18\"><summary>October 18, 2026: Classic travel file repair</summary><div class=\"change-body\"><p>Signed game update 2026101801 adds automatic missing/corrupt terrain and object archive repair for 17 Classic travel destinations, including West Commonlands, Misty Thicket and Toxxulia.</p>\n</div></details><details class=\"change-entry\" id=\"october-17\"><summary>October 17, 2026: progression, combat and crafting</summary><div class=\"change-body\"><ul><li>The optional <a href=\"multiclass.html#recommended-aa\">Recommended AA filter</a> provides an early survival, sustain and damage shortlist across held classes.</li><li>Passive AA is now 10%, preserving full leveling EXP, earned points and 4,000 AA XP per point.</li><li><a href=\"combat.html#monk-cooldowns\">Six basic Monk attacks</a> have separate reuse. <a href=\"combat.html#cooldown-corrections\">Cooldown duration repairs</a> address excessive and restarted timers; other shared identities remain under investigation.</li><li><a href=\"combat.html#death-exp\">Normal death costs no EXP or levels</a>; prior losses are not refunded.</li><li><a href=\"tradeskills.html#stack-limits\">Stackable items support at least 100</a>, retaining larger limits.</li><li>The <a href=\"item-upgrades.html#normal-items\">Reforging Box accepts three identical eligible Normal/Base copies</a> for Polished. Higher recipes still cost four.</li><li>Idle zones can unload without ending their workers and triggering a whole-game restart.</li><li>Update through launcher Play for the matched client.</li></ul>\n</div></details><details class=\"change-entry\" id=\"october-16\"><summary>October 16, 2026</summary><div class=\"change-body\"><ul><li>The <a href=\"dungeon-modes.html#required-bosses\">dungeon guide now lists every required boss</a> and explains boss-stage notices, full-clear credit and Keeper Status when task objectives are blank.</li><li><a href=\"dungeon-modes.html\">Raid and Grind dungeons</a> are deployed with personal boss checklists, shared rewards and exclusive Raid drops.</li><li><a href=\"features.html\">Features</a> now gathers the major departures from Classic.</li><li><a href=\"multiclass.html#equipment-access\">Equipment eligibility</a> recognizes held classes and permits playable races when the class matches; remaining restrictions still apply.</li><li><a href=\"combat.html#buffs\">Temporary AA buffs</a> keep their timers; ordinary blessings remain lasting.</li><li><a href=\"tunnel.html#banking\">Mira Coinwell</a> provides tunnel banking. Haldra stocks Leather Padding.</li><li>The wiki’s guides, commands and generated reward pages have been together against current release evidence.</li></ul>\n</div></details><details class=\"change-entry\" id=\"october-13\"><summary>October 13, 2026</summary><div class=\"change-body\"><ul><li><a href=\"multiclass.html#passive-abilities\">Passive AA changed from 40% to 20%</a>, preserving full normal XP and 4,000 AA XP per point.</li><li><a href=\"multiclass.html#alternate-abilities\">All allowed AA ranks open at level 1</a>; points, eligibility and prerequisite ranks remain.</li><li><a href=\"tradeskills.html\">Stacked tradeskill ingredients and Craft All</a> are deployed.</li><li>The tunnel workshop layout is more spacious; the <a href=\"waypoints.html\">Unrest waypoint</a> moved beside its entrance Keeper.</li><li>Supported divine summoned-hammer families have <a href=\"equipment.html#summoned-gear\">zero resale value</a>.</li><li>The reported multiclass training/offhand issue and merchant Sell All button issue were confirmed resolved.</li></ul>\n</div></details><details class=\"change-entry\" id=\"october-12\"><summary>October 11–12, 2026</summary><div class=\"change-body\"><ul><li><a href=\"item-upgrades.html\">Reusable four-copy upgrades</a> are available from Artisan Veyra; higher #zoneforge steps now use four copies.</li><li><a href=\"equipment.html#free-trade\">LORE restrictions are disabled</a>. Food and drink requirements were removed.</li><li><a href=\"multiclass.html#spell-access\">Early scribing</a> allows eligible scrolls into the spellbook before their casting level.</li><li><a href=\"equipment.html#selling\">Sell All protects food, drink, reagents and casting focus items</a>.</li><li>The launcher uses personal access codes and shows <a href=\"launcher.html#patch-notes\">patch summaries</a>.</li><li>Waypoint portals and floating-eye Instance Keepers received visual corrections. The reported pet-summon crash was confirmed resolved.</li></ul>\n</div></details><details class=\"change-entry\" id=\"october-9\"><summary>October 9, 2026</summary><div class=\"change-body\"><ul><li><a href=\"zones.html\">48 Classic reward zones</a>, <a href=\"items.html\">384 reward variants</a>, type-22 augments and zone forging launched.</li><li>Passive AA increased to 40% at that time; the October 13 reduction above supersedes that rate.</li><li><a href=\"advanced-loot.html#row-controls\">Always Loot / Never Loot controls</a>, effective Spell Damage on <a href=\"combat.html#throw-stone\">Throw Stone</a>, and kept spell gems after normal death were added.</li></ul><p>See In development for candidates. <a href=\"unreleased.html\">More guides</a> </p>\n\n</div></details><h2 id=\"earlier-guide-notices\">Earlier release detail</h2><p>Notices previously repeated across guides are kept below for their original context.</p><details class=\"change-entry\"><summary>Ascension quest: earlier update details</summary><div class=\"change-body\"><h2 id=\"ascension--thj-behavior-candidate\">THJ behavior and stock gear</h2><p>The custom AA, spell focus and stock-derived gear update is. <a href=\"unreleased.html#thj-behavior-candidate\">behavior details and open Play limits</a> </p>\n</div></details><details class=\"change-entry\"><summary>Combat, buffs &amp; recovery: earlier update details</summary><div class=\"change-body\"><p class=\"notice\">Full gear, AA and pet effects are not automatically modeled. <a href=\"build-lab.html\">Try the Build Lab</a> </p>\n<h2 id=\"combat--thj-behavior-candidate\">THJ behavior and stock gear</h2><p>The custom AA, spell focus and stock-derived gear update is. <a href=\"unreleased.html#thj-behavior-candidate\">behavior details and open Play limits</a> </p><p>The update makes Improved Damage, Improved Healing, Mana Preservation, Reagent Conservation and Hate Adjustment use their strongest endpoints.</p>\n<p class=\"notice\">Live AA Play: All 16 classes have more earned AA options: 75 newly available lines, 111 expanded lines and Druid access to Healing Boon. <a href=\"multiclass.html#all-class-aa\">Read the AA update</a> </p>\n<p class=\"notice\">Direct Spell Damage, ordinary DoT ticks, heroic INT/WIS, pet healing and held-class melee effects have changed.</p>\n<h2 id=\"combat--cooldown-corrections\">Cooldown duration repairs</h2><p>Reuse reductions no longer create extremely long lockouts on item clicks, Mend, Bash, Frenzy and linked spells.</p>\n<h2 id=\"combat--blessing-repair\">Blessing effects that survive reconnects</h2><p>Repairs restore saved buff effects after login and stop permanent blessings expiring on the next tick.</p>\n</div></details><details class=\"change-entry\"><summary>Raid &amp; Grind dungeons: earlier update details</summary><div class=\"change-body\"><h2 id=\"dungeon-modes--hole-entrance\">The Hole entrance</h2><p class=\"notice\">— keyless Hole entrance: The Hole Key and lock-picking requirement have been removed from the entrance rock in Paineel at /loc 568,-896,-96.</p>\n<p class=\"notice\" id=\"dungeon-modes--hate-commonlands-candidate\">— Hate Keeper in Commonlands: Find the Plane of Hate Keeper in East Commonlands at /loc -1570,-346,3, between Mirielle and Khalure in the travel area.</p>\n<p class=\"notice\">Keepers offer Raid, Grind, Enter, Join, Status, Claim Rewards and Reset in 21 Classic dungeons. These include Fear, Hate and Sky. </p>\n<h2 id=\"dungeon-modes--classic-candidate\">Every Classic dungeon</h2><p>Added zones: blackburrow, crushbone, runnyeye, soldunga, guktop, gukbottom, mistmoore, kedge, paw, hole, qcat, fearplane, hateplane, airplane.</p><p>Added Raid final bosses receive three dungeon-specific exclusive designs in Polished and Ascended versions.</p>\n<p class=\"notice\">Keeper placement: The overlapping Keepers in Befallen, Unrest, Najena, Permafrost and Nagafen’s Lair now have positions 15 units from their waypoints.</p><table><thead><tr><th>Dungeon</th><th>Keeper /loc</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Befallen</td><td><code>-67,35,3.1</code></td></tr><tr><td>Unrest</td><td><code>-38,67,3.1</code></td></tr><tr><td>Najena</td><td><code>-61,858,4.1</code></td></tr><tr><td>Permafrost</td><td><code>-121,46,2.1</code></td></tr><tr><td>Nagafen’s Lair</td><td><code>-424,-248,-108</code></td></tr><tr><td>High Keep (unchanged)</td><td><code>-16,88,4</code></td></tr><tr><td>Cazic-Thule (unchanged)</td><td><code>71,-74,4</code></td></tr></tbody></table>\n<p class=\"notice\">Selected dungeon equipment budgets are raised so comparable Normal rewards exceed Ascended starter gear.</p>\n<p class=\"notice\">Raid and Grind dungeon modes are available from all 21 dungeon Keepers. <a href=\"dungeon-modes.html\">Raid and Grind dungeon modes</a> </p><p>Raid and Grind choices are available in all 21 Classic combat dungeons listed here, including Fear, Hate and Sky.</p>\n<h2 id=\"dungeon-modes--unique-rewards\">Unique Classic raid rewards</h2><p class=\"notice\">The Classic raid rewards give every dungeon three exclusive designs. <a href=\"dungeon-modes.html#unique-rewards\">Classic raid rewards</a> </p><p>New recommended levels follow each dungeon’s equipment band.</p><p>New numeric power stays within the existing band, slot and quality budgets.</p><table><thead><tr><th>Dungeon / band</th><th>Exclusive designs</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>blackburrow / 20</td><td>Elgnub's Burrowfang<br>Blackburrow Packwarden Mantle<br>Brewer's Amber Seal</td></tr><tr><td>crushbone / 20</td><td>Crush's Broken Scepter<br>Ambassador's Ashen Veil<br>Liberator of the Pens</td></tr><tr><td>runnyeye / 30</td><td>Pickclaw Tunnelbreaker<br>Evil Eye Witness<br>Crown of the Pickclaw Court</td></tr><tr><td>soldunga / 40</td><td>Goblin King's Cinderstaff<br>Firebloom Forgegrips<br>Embervault Reliquary</td></tr><tr><td>guktop / 30</td><td>Shinlord's Oathblade<br>Heart of the Living Guk<br>Reedwoven Watcher Boots</td></tr><tr><td>gukbottom / 50</td><td>Ghoul Lord's Last Decree<br>Pall of the Silent Court<br>Seal of Released Souls</td></tr><tr><td>mistmoore / 40</td><td>Xicotl's Midnight Talon<br>Mistmoore Bloodless Gorget<br>Echo of the Unfinished Waltz</td></tr><tr><td>kedge / 50</td><td>Phinigel's Tidebound Trident<br>Pearl of the Drowned Chorus<br>Kedge Deepcurrent Robe</td></tr><tr><td>paw / 40</td><td>Ishva's Splitpaw Knuckles<br>Splitpaw Spiritcord<br>Denfather Stoneguard</td></tr><tr><td>hole / 50</td><td>Wretched Stonecleaver<br>Pael Sealed Memory<br>Earthbound Oathplate</td></tr><tr><td>qcat / 20</td><td>Omorb's Sluicefang<br>Catacomb Vigil Lantern<br>Qeynos Underway Satchel</td></tr><tr><td>fearplane / 50</td><td>Spine of the Faceless<br>Visage of Unbroken Will<br>Dreadhusk of the Last Stand</td></tr><tr><td>hateplane / 50</td><td>Innoruuk's Severed Covenant<br>Maestro's Unfinished Requiem<br>Seal of the First Betrayal</td></tr><tr><td>airplane / 50</td><td>Veeshan's Unwritten Horizon<br>Mantle of the First Brood<br>Astrolabe of the Eighth Island</td></tr></tbody></table><h3>Planar relics</h3><p>Fear: Visage of Unbroken Will reveals the unseen with See Invisible, beside Spine of the Faceless and Dreadhusk of the Last Stand.</p><p>Hate: Maestro’s Unfinished Requiem grants Invisibility; Innoruuk’s Severed Covenant and Seal of the First Betrayal recall hatred and broken elven royalty.</p><p>Sky: Astrolabe of the Eighth Island grants ordinary Levitate, beside Veeshan’s Unwritten Horizon and Mantle of the First Brood.</p><p>Each click requires equipping the item at level 46 and a ten-second cast.</p></div></details><details class=\"change-entry\"><summary>Equipment &amp; trading: earlier update details</summary><div class=\"change-body\"><h2 id=\"equipment--loot-finder-preview\">Find ordinary equipment</h2><p>Use the loot finder to match your held classes and locate database-dropped equipment within the active era. <a href=\"loot-finder.html\">loot finder</a> <a href=\"items.html\">Hunt catalog</a> </p><p class=\"notice\">Full gear, AA and pet effects are not automatically modeled. <a href=\"build-lab.html\">Try the Build Lab</a> </p>\n<p class=\"notice\">The Classic raid rewards give every dungeon three exclusive designs. <a href=\"dungeon-modes.html#unique-rewards\">Classic raid rewards</a> </p>\n<h2 id=\"equipment--quest-ingredients\">Quest ingredient qualities -</h2><p>Normal-item quest requirements accept Polished, Exalted and Ascended versions of the same item.</p>\n<h2 id=\"equipment--classic-robes\">Classic race robes</h2><p>Game update 2026102204 repairs the model binding behind the waist gap reported on Barbarian and Half Elf.</p>\n<h2 id=\"equipment--thj-behavior-candidate\">THJ behavior and stock gear</h2><p>The custom AA, spell focus and stock-derived gear update is. <a href=\"unreleased.html#thj-behavior-candidate\">behavior details and open Play limits</a> </p><p>The update uses unmodified stock ProjectEQ as an approximation of standard EverQuest, then preserves the exact researched values where available.</p><table><thead><tr><th>Ascended field</th><th>Target from stock</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Positive AC, HP, mana, primary stats, resists, weapon damage and HP/mana regeneration</td><td>2×</td></tr><tr><td>Haste</td><td>1.5×, rounded</td></tr><tr><td>Spell Damage when stock has none</td><td>Higher of 2× INT or WIS</td></tr><tr><td>Healing Amount when stock has none</td><td>2× WIS</td></tr><tr><td>Accuracy when stock has none</td><td>Half DEX, rounded upward</td></tr><tr><td>New heroics</td><td>Quarter of the final matching stat, rounded; Ascended only</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Polished and Exalted receive one-third and two-thirds of the increase from Normal to Ascended.</p>\n<p class=\"notice\">Selected Ascended items now use THJ values, including reductions.</p>\n<p class=\"notice\">Browse the equipment catalog → Find a reward by slot, required level or source zone, with all four qualities grouped together. <a href=\"items.html\">Browse the equipment catalog →</a> </p></div></details><details class=\"change-entry\"><summary>Features: earlier update details</summary><div class=\"change-body\"><h2 id=\"features--hole-entrance\">The Hole entrance</h2><p class=\"notice\">— keyless Hole entrance: The Hole Key and lock-picking requirement have been removed from the entrance rock in Paineel at /loc 568,-896,-96.</p>\n<h2 id=\"features--loot-finder-preview\">Plan equipment for your classes</h2><p>The loot finder matches equipment usable by any held class, with an optional all-selected-classes mode, active-era filtering and source mobs, locations and calculated drop chances. <a href=\"loot-finder.html\">loot finder</a> </p><p class=\"notice\" id=\"features--hate-commonlands-candidate\">— Hate Keeper in Commonlands: Find the Plane of Hate Keeper in East Commonlands at /loc -1570,-346,3, between Mirielle and Khalure in the travel area.</p>\n<p class=\"notice\">Full gear, AA and pet effects are not automatically modeled. <a href=\"build-lab.html\">Try the Build Lab</a> </p>\n<p class=\"notice\">The Classic raid rewards give every dungeon three exclusive designs. <a href=\"dungeon-modes.html#unique-rewards\">Classic raid rewards</a> </p>\n<p class=\"notice\">Every Classic dungeon coverage adds the same Raid/Grind choices in 21 combat dungeon zones, including Fear, Hate and Sky. <a href=\"dungeon-modes.html#classic-candidate\">Every Classic dungeon coverage</a> </p>\n<h2 id=\"features--quest-ingredients-candidate\">Quest ingredient qualities -</h2><p>Better ordinary qualities can satisfy Normal quest ingredients, including the Aviak Charm for Crafted Gauntlets. <a href=\"equipment.html#quest-ingredients\">ingredient rules and limits</a> </p>\n<p class=\"notice\">Five class-armor families now give guaranteed Ascended rewards. <a href=\"unreleased.html#quest-quality\">guaranteed Ascended rewards</a> </p>\n<p class=\"notice\">Game update 2026102204 repairs the waist binding in the robe bodies added for seven Classic races. <a href=\"equipment.html#classic-robes\">Robe update</a> </p>\n<p class=\"notice\">Level-scaled AA: Earn two AA per level while leveling. <a href=\"multiclass.html#passive-abilities\">AA progression and examples</a> </p>\n<h2 id=\"features--thj-behavior-candidate\">THJ behavior and stock gear</h2><p>The custom AA, spell focus and stock-derived gear update is. <a href=\"unreleased.html#thj-behavior-candidate\">behavior details and open Play limits</a> </p>\n<p class=\"notice\">Live AA Play: All 16 classes have more earned AA options: 75 newly available lines, 111 expanded lines and Druid access to Healing Boon. <a href=\"multiclass.html#all-class-aa\">Read the AA update</a> </p>\n<p class=\"notice\">The combined item, spell, pet equipment and melee release is.</p>\n<p>Ordinary eligible equipment and bags have a 20% Polished, 5% Exalted and 1% Ascended chance per drop. <a href=\"equipment.html#item-tiers\">Read the loot quality rules</a> </p>\n<p class=\"feature-intro\">The major departures from Classic, with the rules you need before your next adventure.</p><p class=\"notice\"> <a href=\"unreleased.html\">More guides</a> </p><h2 id=\"features--character\">Build one character from three classes</h2><div class=\"feature-list\"><section class=\"feature-row\"><h3>Three classes from level 1</h3><div><p>Keep your starting class and choose two different extra classes.</p><a href=\"multiclass.html#three-classes\">Choose your classes →</a></div></section><section class=\"feature-row\"><h3>AA progression from the beginning</h3><div><p>Allowed AA ranks open at level 1.</p><a href=\"multiclass.html#passive-abilities\">Understand AA progression →</a></div></section><section class=\"feature-row\"><h3>Scribe spells ahead of time</h3><div><p>Eligible scrolls can enter your spellbook early.</p><a href=\"multiclass.html#spell-access\">Learn the spell rules →</a></div></section><section class=\"feature-row\"><h3>A roster of companions</h3><div><p>Multiple summoned pets, selected-pet or All-pets commands, and stored pet armor support a multiclass roster.</p><a href=\"pets.html\">Manage your pets →</a></div></section></div><h2 id=\"features--rewards\">Earn, trade and upgrade your gear</h2><div class=\"feature-list\"><section class=\"feature-row\"><h3>Stronger item qualities and zone rewards</h3><div><p>Ordinary tiered gear and the 48-zone reward hunt offer distinct quality families.</p><a href=\"zone-hunt.html\">Explore rewards and sockets →</a></div></section><section class=\"feature-row\"><h3>Turn duplicates into upgrades</h3><div><p>Use three Base zone rewards for Polished, then four matching copies for each higher step. <a href=\"item-upgrades.html#normal-items\">three identical eligible Normal/Base copies for Polished</a> </p><a href=\"item-upgrades.html\">See the upgrade recipes →</a></div></section><section class=\"feature-row\"><h3>Free trading and no LORE limit</h3><div><p>Trade formerly restricted and attuned items and keep duplicate LORE items.</p><a href=\"equipment.html#free-trade\">Read trading and resale rules →</a></div></section><section class=\"feature-row\"><h3>Equipment for your held classes</h3><div><p>Wear ordinary equipment allowed by any held class, regardless of playable race.</p><a href=\"multiclass.html#equipment-access\">Check equipment eligibility →</a></div></section></div><h2 id=\"features--adventuring\">Prepare in the tunnel, then explore</h2><div class=\"feature-list\"><section class=\"feature-row\"><h3>Raid or Grind in all 21 Classic dungeons</h3><div><p>Choose normal respawning enemies or harder enemies with permanent deaths.</p><a href=\"dungeon-modes.html\">Choose your dungeon mode →</a></div></section><section class=\"feature-row\"><h3>A shared home base</h3><div><p>New characters start with a kit and 100 platinum in the East Commonlands tunnel.</p><a href=\"tunnel.html\">Meet the tunnel services →</a></div></section><section class=\"feature-row\"><h3>Travel, discovery and private dungeons</h3><div><p>Use tunnel travel services, discover waypoint destinations and enter supported personal dungeon instances.</p><a href=\"travel.html\">Plan your journey →</a></div></section><section class=\"feature-row\"><h3>Lasting blessings; temporary combat abilities</h3><div><p>Ordinary beneficial blessings persist on players and owned pets.</p><a href=\"combat.html#buffs\">Know which effects last →</a></div></section><section class=\"feature-row\"><h3>Keep fighting while you cast</h3><div><p>Damage-over-time spells cast instantly, and melee autoattacks can continue during casting.</p><a href=\"combat.html#casting\">Read the combat changes →</a></div></section><section class=\"feature-row\"><h3>Less upkeep between adventures</h3><div><p>Food and drink are optional.</p><a href=\"combat.html\">Read combat and recovery →</a></div></section><section class=\"feature-row\"><h3>Healing without changing your target</h3><div><p>Ordinary heals can heal your own permanent pet.</p><a href=\"combat.html#healing\">Check healing targets →</a></div></section></div><h2 id=\"features--tools\">Spend more time playing</h2><div class=\"feature-list\"><section class=\"feature-row\"><h3>Stacked materials and Craft All</h3><div><p>Stackable items support at least 100, preserving larger limits.</p><a href=\"tradeskills.html\">Use the crafting controls →</a></div></section><section class=\"feature-row\"><h3>Advanced loot and bulk selling</h3><div><p>Use personal loot queues, loot preferences and group rolls.</p><a href=\"advanced-loot.html\">Learn the loot interface →</a></div></section><section class=\"feature-row\"><h3>One launcher, current updates</h3><div><p>The normal Nightcap shortcut delivers managed game/interface updates and dated patch summaries.</p><a href=\"launcher.html\">Update before playing →</a></div></section></div><h2 id=\"features--updates\">Keep up with changes</h2><p>Read Recent changes for dated updates. <a href=\"recent-changes.html\">Recent changes</a> </p><p class=\"notice\">Raid and Grind dungeon modes are available from all 21 dungeon Keepers. <a href=\"dungeon-modes.html\">Raid and Grind dungeon modes</a> </p>\n\n\n<h2 id=\"features--october-improvements\">More guidance and independent attacks</h2><p>The optional Recommended AA filter helps you choose early survival and damage upgrades. <a href=\"multiclass.html#recommended-aa\">Recommended AA filter</a> <a href=\"combat.html#monk-cooldowns\">Six basic Monk attacks have separate cooldowns</a> </p>\n<h2 id=\"features--thj-scaling\">Item and spell progression</h2><p>Ascended items, modest starter upgrades and stronger dungeon budgets bring item progression closer to the observed THJ references. <a href=\"equipment.html#reviewed-ascended\">Ascended items</a> <a href=\"combat.html#spell-scaling\">Additive Spell Damage and direct heroic-stat bonuses</a> </p>\n\n<h2 id=\"features--chapterhouse-candidate\">The Vigil of the Dawn</h2><p>Camil’s level-50 Paladin story in Chapterhouse uses Tasks, persistent personal chapters and a one-time helmet claim. <a href=\"camil-vigil.html\">Read the quest guide</a> <a href=\"zone-chapterhouse.html\">reward catalog</a> </p>\n</div></details><details class=\"change-entry\"><summary>Getting started: earlier update details</summary><div class=\"change-body\"><p class=\"notice\">Level-scaled AA: Earn two AA per level while leveling. <a href=\"multiclass.html#passive-abilities\">AA progression and examples</a> </p>\n<h2 id=\"getting-started--thj-behavior-candidate\">THJ behavior and stock gear</h2><p>The custom AA, spell focus and stock-derived gear update is. <a href=\"unreleased.html#thj-behavior-candidate\">behavior details and open Play limits</a> </p>\n<p class=\"notice\">Starter equipment now has modest quality upgrades.</p>\n<h2 id=\"getting-started--travel-files\">Repair missing Classic zone files</h2><p>Use the usual launcher Play flow for the Classic travel archive repair. <a href=\"launcher.html#zone-repair\">Classic travel archive repair</a> </p>\n<p>Nightcap is a solo-preferred progression server: thoughtful preparation, earned gear and encounter execution matter.</p>\n<p>Read Features first for the major ways Nightcap differs from Classic. <a href=\"features.html\">Read Features first</a> </p></div></details><details class=\"change-entry\"><summary>Welcome to the Nightcap Wiki: earlier update details</summary><div class=\"change-body\"><h2 id=\"index--hole-entrance\">The Hole entrance</h2><p class=\"notice\">— keyless Hole entrance: The Hole Key and lock-picking requirement have been removed from the entrance rock in Paineel at /loc 568,-896,-96.</p>\n<h2 id=\"index--loot-finder-preview\">Find your next upgrade</h2><p>Choose up to three held classes and find current-era equipment, its source mobs, locations and calculated drop chances. <a href=\"loot-finder.html\">Open the loot finder</a> </p><p class=\"notice\" id=\"index--hate-commonlands-candidate\">— Hate Keeper in Commonlands: Find the Plane of Hate Keeper in East Commonlands at /loc -1570,-346,3, between Mirielle and Khalure in the travel area.</p>\n<p class=\"notice\">The Classic raid rewards give every dungeon three exclusive designs. <a href=\"dungeon-modes.html#unique-rewards\">Classic raid rewards</a> </p>\n<p class=\"notice\">Every Classic dungeon coverage adds the same Raid/Grind choices in 21 combat dungeon zones, including Fear, Hate and Sky. <a href=\"dungeon-modes.html#classic-candidate\">Every Classic dungeon coverage</a> </p>\n<h2 id=\"index--quest-ingredients-candidate\">quest ingredient qualities</h2><p>Quest hand-ins and deliveries now accept Polished, Exalted and Ascended versions of Normal ingredients. <a href=\"equipment.html#quest-ingredients\">Try the Crafted Gauntlets turn-in and review the limits</a> </p>\n<p class=\"notice\">Crafted and four other class-armor families now award Ascended gear. <a href=\"unreleased.html#quest-quality\">Crafted and four other class-armor families</a> </p>\n<p class=\"notice\">The Classic robe waist correction is available for seven races. <a href=\"equipment.html#classic-robes\">Classic robe waist correction</a> </p>\n<p class=\"notice\">Level-scaled AA: Earn two AA per level while leveling. <a href=\"multiclass.html#passive-abilities\">AA progression and examples</a> </p>\n<h2 id=\"index--thj-behavior-candidate\">THJ behavior and stock gear</h2><p>The custom AA, spell focus and stock-derived gear update is. <a href=\"unreleased.html#thj-behavior-candidate\">behavior details and open Play limits</a> </p>\n<p class=\"notice\">Live AA Play: All 16 classes have more earned AA options: 75 newly available lines, 111 expanded lines and Druid access to Healing Boon. <a href=\"multiclass.html#all-class-aa\">Read the AA update</a> </p>\n<p class=\"notice\">Launch repair published: Game update 2026101901 corrects the client catalog mismatch that blocked Play after the previous update.</p>\n<p class=\"notice\">The item/spell and pet/melee release is available.</p>\n<p>Ordinary loot quality chances are now 20% Polished, 5% Exalted and 1% Ascended per eligible item drop. <a href=\"equipment.html#item-tiers\">Loot quality details</a> </p><p class=\"notice\">October 18 update:Independent AA cooldowns and item/discipline timer repairs are available. <a href=\"combat.html#ability-cooldowns\">Independent AA cooldowns and item/discipline timer repairs</a> </p><p>October 18:Classic travel archive repair is available through normal launcher Play, including West Commonlands. <a href=\"launcher.html#zone-repair\">Classic travel archive repair</a> </p>\n<p class=\"notice\">October 17 update:Recommended AA, passive AA while leveling, no normal-death EXP loss, stacks of at least 100, three-Normal reforging and independent Monk attacks are available. <a href=\"multiclass.html#recommended-aa\">Recommended AA</a> <a href=\"combat.html#death-exp\">no normal-death EXP loss</a> </p>\n<div class=\"welcome\"><div class=\"welcome-copy\"><p class=\"eyebrow\">A familiar world.</p><h2>Three classes.<br>One more adventure.</h2><p>Find your build, learn the custom systems, and discover what is waiting beyond the tunnel.</p><a class=\"button\" href=\"getting-started.html\">Start your journey →</a></div><img src=\"assets/traders-at-dusk.png\" width=\"1672\" height=\"941\" alt=\"Nightcap traders beneath lanterns in a stone tunnel at dusk.\"></div><div class=\"facts\"><span><strong>Classic</strong> current era</span><span><strong>50</strong> level cap</span><span><strong>3</strong> classes per character</span><span><strong>48</strong> reward zones</span></div><p class=\"feature-entry\">New to Nightcap?Explore Features — the major changes from Classic → <a href=\"features.html\">Explore Features — the major changes from Classic →</a> </p><div class=\"portal-grid\"><section class=\"portal\"><h2>Character &amp; classes</h2><ul><li><a href=\"multiclass.html\">Multiclass &amp; progression</a><small>Choose your classes, skills and abilities.</small></li><li><a href=\"pets.html\">Pets &amp; pet armor</a><small>Your companions, commands and loadouts.</small></li></ul></section><section class=\"portal\"><h2>Items &amp; equipment</h2><ul><li><a href=\"items.html\">Browse equipment</a><small>Find gear and augments by slot, level and zone.</small></li><li><a href=\"zone-hunt.html\">Zone hunt &amp; forging</a><small>Drop chances, heroic augments and upgrades.</small></li><li><a href=\"equipment.html\">Equipment &amp; trading</a><small>Existing tiers, bags and selling rules.</small></li></ul></section><section class=\"portal\"><h2>Explore the world</h2><ul><li><a href=\"zones.html\">Zones &amp; rewards</a><small>48 Classic destinations and their rewards.</small></li><li><a href=\"tunnel.html\">East Commonlands tunnel</a><small>Trainers, merchants and blessings.</small></li><li><a href=\"travel.html\">Travel &amp; instances</a><small>Find your way out. Find your way home.</small></li></ul></section><section class=\"portal\"><h2>Adventures &amp; quests</h2><ul><li><a href=\"advanced-loot.html\">Advanced loot</a><small>Personal drops, filters and group rolls.</small></li><li><a href=\"ascension.html\">Ascension quest</a><small>Reforge your original class epic.</small></li><li><a href=\"waypoints.html\">Waypoint Explorer</a><small>Discover destinations and earn a title.</small></li></ul></section></div><div class=\"home-columns\"><section><h2>New in Nightcap</h2><p>Raid or Grind in all 21 Classic dungeons. <a href=\"dungeon-modes.html\">Raid or Grind in all 21 Classic dungeons.</a> </p><p>Build, craft and upgrade. <a href=\"item-upgrades.html#normal-items\">normal-item box recipe</a> </p><p>Passive AA is now 10% alongside normal leveling. <a href=\"recent-changes.html\">Guide</a> </p></section><section><h2>At the campfire</h2><ul><li><a href=\"commands.html\">Keep the command reference handy</a></li><li><a href=\"launcher.html\">Update your launcher and game</a></li><li><a href=\"combat.html\">Read about combat and recovery</a></li><li><a href=\"unreleased.html\">See what is still in development</a></li></ul><p class=\"notice\">Nightcap is available.</p></section></div>\n\n\n\n<h2 id=\"index--chapterhouse-candidate\">The Vigil of the Dawn</h2><p>Camil’s Vigil of the Dawn is available. <a href=\"camil-vigil.html\">Read the quest guide</a> <a href=\"zone-chapterhouse.html\">reward catalog</a> </p>\n</div></details><details class=\"change-entry\"><summary>Item upgrades: earlier update details</summary><div class=\"change-body\"><h2 id=\"item-upgrades--quest-ingredients-candidate\">Quest ingredient qualities -</h2><p>Ordinary quality variants can satisfy Normal quest requirements. <a href=\"equipment.html#quest-ingredients\">Ordinary quality variants can satisfy Normal quest requirements</a> </p>\n<h2 id=\"item-upgrades--thj-behavior-candidate\">THJ behavior and stock gear</h2><p>The custom AA, spell focus and stock-derived gear update is. <a href=\"unreleased.html#thj-behavior-candidate\">behavior details and open Play limits</a> </p><p>The update changes stats on existing ordinary qualities.</p>\n<p class=\"notice\">Selected Ascended values and intermediate stats have been retuned while retaining item identities, effects and sockets.</p>\n<p>Nightcap has two forgeable tier families: ordinary tiered equipment ends at Ascended, while the Classic zone-hunt rewards end at Ascension.</p>\n</div></details><details class=\"change-entry\"><summary>Launcher &amp; interface: earlier update details</summary><div class=\"change-body\"><h2 id=\"launcher--classic-robes-candidate\">Classic robe waist correction</h2><p>Game update 2026102204 repairs model binding on the added Classic robe bodies after the earlier 2026102203 repair failed. <a href=\"equipment.html#classic-robes\">Affected races and Play status</a> </p>\n<p class=\"notice\">Launch repair published: Game update 2026101901 corrects the client catalog mismatch that blocked Play after the previous update.</p>\n<p class=\"notice\">Game update 2026101802 pairs the expanded pet Equipment tab and spell/AA descriptions with the new server release.</p>\n<h2 id=\"launcher--zone-repair\">Classic travel file checks</h2><p>Game update 2026101801 adds terrain and object archive checks for 17 Classic travel destinations, including West Commonlands, Misty Thicket and Toxxulia.</p>\n<h2 id=\"launcher--startup-repairs\">Startup and character-selection repairs</h2><p>Updates repair model archives and missing materials behind the recent Play and character-selection failures.</p>\n<h2 id=\"launcher--animation-repairs\">Creature and pet animation repairs</h2><p>The latest updates repair shared creature animations and Enchanter weapon-pet identity.</p>\n\n<h2 id=\"launcher--october-release\">October 17 gameplay update</h2><p>Close EverQuest and choose Play to receive the Recommended AA window and independent Monk attack timers.</p></div></details><details class=\"change-entry\"><summary>Multiclass &amp; progression: earlier update details</summary><div class=\"change-body\"><h2 id=\"multiclass--loot-finder-preview\">Search gear for your held classes</h2><p>The loot finder defaults to Any held class, matching Nightcap equipment access. <a href=\"loot-finder.html\">loot finder</a> </p><p class=\"notice\">Robe appearance: Game update 2026102204 repairs the robe waist binding for seven Classic races. <a href=\"equipment.html#classic-robes\">Affected races and Play status</a> </p>\n<p class=\"notice\">Level-scaled AA: Earn two AA per level while leveling. <a href=\"multiclass.html#passive-abilities\">AA progression and examples</a> </p>\n<h2 id=\"multiclass--thj-behavior-candidate\">THJ behavior and stock gear</h2><p>The custom AA, spell focus and stock-derived gear update is. <a href=\"unreleased.html#thj-behavior-candidate\">behavior details and open Play limits</a> </p><p>AA changes include group Act of Valor, 40% Harvest and percentage-based Mana Burn. Silent Casting, Warrior debuffs and Wizard abilities also change. </p>\n<p class=\"notice\">Live AA Play: All 16 classes have more earned AA options: 75 newly available lines, 111 expanded lines and Druid access to Healing Boon. <a href=\"multiclass.html#all-class-aa\">Read the AA update</a> </p>\n<p class=\"notice\">earned pet and melee AA ranks and held-class combat benefits are available.</p>\n</div></details><details class=\"change-entry\"><summary>Pets &amp; pet armor: earlier update details</summary><div class=\"change-body\"><h2 id=\"pets--thj-behavior-candidate\">THJ behavior and stock gear</h2><p>The custom AA, spell focus and stock-derived gear update is. <a href=\"unreleased.html#thj-behavior-candidate\">behavior details and open Play limits</a> </p><p>The focus changes apply to players and permanent pets.</p>\n<p class=\"notice\">Permanent-pet equipment has three pages with 22 locations. Mage pets can hold 15 items. Other permanent class pets can hold eight. </p>\n</div></details><details class=\"change-entry\"><summary>Travel &amp; instances: earlier update details</summary><div class=\"change-body\"><h2 id=\"travel--hole-entrance\">The Hole entrance</h2><p class=\"notice\">— keyless Hole entrance: The Hole Key and lock-picking requirement have been removed from the entrance rock in Paineel at /loc 568,-896,-96.</p>\n<p class=\"notice\" id=\"travel--hate-commonlands-candidate\">— Hate Keeper in Commonlands: Find the Plane of Hate Keeper in East Commonlands at /loc -1570,-346,3, between Mirielle and Khalure in the travel area.</p>\n<p class=\"notice\">The Classic raid rewards give every dungeon three exclusive designs. <a href=\"dungeon-modes.html#unique-rewards\">Classic raid rewards</a> </p>\n<p class=\"notice\">Every Classic dungeon coverage adds the same Raid/Grind choices in 21 combat dungeon zones, including Fear, Hate and Sky. <a href=\"dungeon-modes.html#classic-candidate\">Every Classic dungeon coverage</a> </p>\n<p class=\"notice\">The separate level-65/Planes of Power profile and its additional merchant stock remain staged.</p>\n<h2 id=\"travel--missing-zone-files\">If a Classic destination fails to load</h2><p>Close EverQuest and use launcher Play to install game update 2026101801 or newer.</p>\n</div></details><details class=\"change-entry\"><summary>East Commonlands tunnel: earlier update details</summary><div class=\"change-body\"><h2 id=\"tunnel--experience-blessing\">XP blessing retired</h2><p>Magus Goldwind no longer charges platinum or grants the XP package.</p>\n</div></details><details class=\"change-entry\"><summary>More guides: earlier update details</summary><div class=\"change-body\"><p class=\"notice\" id=\"unreleased--hate-commonlands-candidate\">— Hate Keeper in Commonlands: Find the Plane of Hate Keeper in East Commonlands at /loc -1570,-346,3, between Mirielle and Khalure in the travel area.</p>\n<p class=\"notice\">The Classic raid rewards give every dungeon three exclusive designs. <a href=\"dungeon-modes.html#unique-rewards\">Classic raid rewards</a> </p>\n<p class=\"notice\">Every Classic dungeon coverage adds the same Raid/Grind choices in 21 combat dungeon zones, including Fear, Hate and Sky. <a href=\"dungeon-modes.html#classic-candidate\">Every Classic dungeon coverage</a> </p>\n<h2 id=\"unreleased--quest-ingredients\">Quest ingredient qualities -</h2><p>The fix for rejection of Aviak Charm (Polished) is deployed. <a href=\"equipment.html#quest-ingredients\">explicit-quality and forging rules remain separate</a> </p>\n<h2 id=\"unreleased--crystal-markers\">Waypoint crystals</h2><p>Waypoints now have a glowing crystal with the existing a waypoint label.</p>\n<h2 id=\"unreleased--classic-robes\">Classic robe waist correction</h2><p>Game update 2026102204 repairs the waist binding after the earlier 2026102203 repair failed on Barbarian and Half Elf. <a href=\"equipment.html#classic-robes\">Update details</a> </p>\n<h2 id=\"unreleased--befallen-keeper\">Dungeon Keeper visibility</h2><p>The placement correction now covers all five confirmed waypoint overlaps: Befallen, Unrest, Najena, Permafrost and Nagafen’s Lair. <a href=\"dungeon-modes.html\">Keeper locations</a> </p>\n<h2 id=\"unreleased--thj-behavior-candidate\">THJ behavior and stock gear</h2><p>The custom AA, spell focus and stock-derived gear update is. <a href=\"unreleased.html#thj-behavior-candidate\">behavior details and open Play limits</a> </p><h3>Custom AA behavior</h3><ul><li>Warlord’s Fury: +100% physical skill damage for up to 12 seconds, 60-second reuse.</li><li>Gut Punch: initial damage and +50% physical damage taken for up to 12 seconds. Press the Attack lowers AC; Grappling Strike lowers evasion. </li><li>Act of Valor: spends 50% of maximum mana once and heals nearby group members for 2 HP per mana spent.</li><li>Harvest: activate to restore 40% maximum mana.</li><li>Mana Burn/Blast/Blaze/Volatile Mana Blaze: spend 10/20/30/40% maximum mana; keep 4 damage per mana as a tuning choice. All reach 15-minute reuse with full Hastened Manaburn. Target immunity rejects the cast without mana or cooldown loss.</li><li>Silent Casting: all casting classes, one-hour duration, 60-second reuse, suspendable timer. Subtlety and obsolete haste/duration modifiers refund purchased ranks.</li><li>Dimensional Shielding: separate Wizard AA protecting casting from hits, movement and hostile interrupt effects. Stuns and voluntary cancellation still interrupt. Its 120-second duration and 30-minute reuse are kept-value tuning choices.</li><li>Pyromancy/Cryomancy: 35% proc chance, initial damage plus DoT, opposite-element resistance reduction and compatibility with other buffs. Existing level/mana/trigger restrictions remain.</li></ul><h3>Evidence and Play limits</h3><p>The stock baseline is ProjectEQ, not a recovered THJ or Daybreak database.</p>\n<h2 id=\"unreleased--all-class-aa\">All-class AAs are now in</h2><p>The rank and access update is installed. <a href=\"multiclass.html#all-class-aa\">the released AA rules</a> </p>\n<h2 id=\"unreleased--thj-parity\">Item and spell scaling is now in</h2><p>The combined release is installed. <a href=\"equipment.html\">Equipment</a> <a href=\"combat.html\">Combat</a> </p><h2 id=\"unreleased--wpm-melee\">Shield and melee changes are now in</h2><p>The earned held-class melee and shield changes shipped with the combined release. <a href=\"combat.html#melee-builds\">the combat guide</a> </p><h2 id=\"unreleased--pet-scaling\">Separate level-65 and Planes of Power profile</h2><p>The expanded pet equipment and scaling changes are installed, but the level-65/Planes of Power profile and 389 additional merchant entries are still staged.</p>\n<h2 id=\"unreleased--quest-quality\">Guaranteed quality for substantial class armor</h2><p>The installed update grants existing Ascended versions of 37 Crafted, Lambent, Darkforge, Ivy Etched and Totemic quest rewards.</p><p>The 37 rewards are live.</p><h2 id=\"unreleased--cooldown-identities\">Remaining shared skill and spell cooldowns</h2><p>The AA and cross-ability timer correction is deployed. <a href=\"combat.html#ability-cooldowns\">AA and cross-ability timer correction is deployed</a> </p>\n<h2 id=\"unreleased--journal\">Adventure Journal prototype — historical status</h2><p>The original eight quests and charm were built as an uninstalled prototype. <a href=\"#last-lantern-20261107\">November7 Last Lantern release</a> </p>\n<h2 id=\"unreleased--combat\">Combat and item candidates</h2><p>The separate extra-class skill, trainer and offhand correction is deployed; the reported player issue was confirmed resolved. <a href=\"multiclass.html#earned-skills\">extra-class skill, trainer and offhand correction</a> </p>\n<h2 id=\"unreleased--testing\">System guides</h2><p>See Features for the available systems. <a href=\"features.html\">Features</a> </p>\n\n<h2 id=\"unreleased--chapterhouse-candidate\">The Vigil of the Dawn</h2><p>The Vigil of the Dawn has moved into. <a href=\"camil-vigil.html\">Read the quest guide</a> <a href=\"zone-chapterhouse.html\">reward catalog</a> </p>\n</div></details><details class=\"change-entry\"><summary>Waypoint Explorer: earlier update details</summary><div class=\"change-body\"><h2 id=\"waypoints--crystal-markers\">Waypoint crystals</h2><p>Waypoints now have a glowing crystal with the existing a waypoint label.</p>\n</div></details>\n\n<h2 id=\"paladin-weapon-grip-20261026\">October 26, 2026 — Paladin weapon grips</h2><p>a right-click 1HS/2HS toggle is available for SoulFire, Fiery Avenger and Fiery Defender, including existing quality variants. <a href=\"equipment.html#paladin-weapon-grip\">Grip instructions</a> </p>\n<h2 id=\"paladin-grip-repair-20261027\">October27 grip issue and October28 paired repair</h2><p>SoulFire could report 1HS while the client kept a two-handed definition. <a href=\"equipment.html#paladin-weapon-grip\">Stats and grip instructions</a> </p><h2 id=\"bazaar-ui-repair-20261028\">October28 — missing Bazaar controls</h2><p>The update also corrects a Bazaar XML parsing error that made the entire Nightcap interface fall back to Default.</p>\n<h2 id=\"bazaar-startup-crash-20261028\">October 28: Bazaar startup crash — client hotfix 2026102802</h2><p>Client hotfix 2026102802 corrects missing Bazaar tab borders that caused a crash during world entry.</p>\n<h2 id=\"hate-layout-20261029\">October 29: Plane of Hate ground-level layout</h2><p>New Raid and Grind runs use the newer Hate layout. Existing encounters, enemy strength, loot, experience and completion rewards remain. <a href=\"dungeon-modes.html#hate-layout-preview\">Entry and landmarks</a> </p>\n\n<h2 id=\"keyless-doors-20261029\">October 29: keyless doors</h2><p>Keys and lock picks are no longer required for ordinary locked doors throughout existing door content. <a href=\"travel.html#keyless-doors\">Door access and remaining restrictions</a> </p>\n\n\n<h2 id=\"cast-bar-repair-20261030\">October 30: spell casting bar timing — reported issue resolved</h2><p>Client update 2026103002 corrects casting bars that stayed full until the final instant. <a href=\"launcher.html#cast-bar-repair\">Update instructions</a> </p>\n<h2 id=\"hate-boss-placement-20261030\">October 30: Hate boss landmark correction</h2><p>Corrected the ground-level substitute locations for Maestro, the Hand and Innoruuk to their organ/platform/throne landmarks.</p>\n\n<h2 id=\"augment-description-correction\">November6: augment descriptions and equipped totals</h2><p>Client0.13.3 shows Hunt Shield Block in the item Description with its shield and strongest-only restrictions. <a href=\"augment-audit.html#augment-description-correction\">Instructions and stacking</a> </p>\n<h2 id=\"augment-icon-candidate\">November 12: augment icon correction</h2><p>Ordinary stat augments now preserve equipment icons and existing cosmetic transformations. <a href=\"equipment.html#augment-icon-candidate\">Equipment guidance</a> </p><h2 id=\"earned-titles-20261112\">November 12: earned titles</h2><p>A Titles reference describes 77 cosmetic unlocks and their exact requirements. <a href=\"titles.html\">Titles reference</a> </p>",
